  "JOURNAL_Lore_Drops": {
    "Goblin_B3": "13 Wintumber 4209\r\n\r\nIt’s cold this time of year, though not as cold as the legends say. Perhaps Ashenfall’s climate is warm and pleasant. Maybe the magic of this place keeps the winter at bay?\r\n\r\nThere was a snowfall, heavy and solid, that trapped me in this place. I warmed myself by the fire and another joined me. The goblin, Globfinger and he’s more pleasant than his name suggests. He came in out of the cold and in the spirit of our people’s alliance, I shared a warm meal with him.\r\n\r\nWe spoke of battles, as goblins always do. I wonder if they know of any other activity other than conflict, yet if they do, they dare not speak of it. We regailed one another with tales of fights against the wildfolk, as goblin and human cut down the beasts.\r\n\r\nGoblins may be uncouth, undisciplined and smelly, but they celebrate well. We laughed with one another and cheered on our clans. He told me he is glad that his god had beef to settle with the moon-goddess, otherwise we would not have had such an enjoyable war.\r\n\r\nHe’s right. I have enjoyed a righteous cause.\r\n\r\nPerhaps, goblins aren’t so bad.",
    "DragonAttack_A1": "17 Novtumber 4207\r\n\r\nI miss the monastery, with its moss-covered walls and the chill breeze that spreads to your bones. They don't have that here. The Ashenfall breeze is strong and cold, but it seeps into your bones and causes shakes, not shivers. It's the sort of cold that acts as a warning.\r\n\r\nI think this whole continent is out to get us. I just wanted to preach the blessed teachings of Saradomin in the warm comfort of a nice church made of stone not wood.\r\n\r\nI miss the city, with it’s bustle, noise and smell. The crisp country air is too sterile for me.\r\n\r\nStill, I'm here to save the souls of the lost. In this age of constant conflict, it's nice to find a small village that just needs a sermon or two. \r\n\r\nWe shall bring into the light of Saradomin's truth. They seem eager, abandoned as they are by their pagan patron, but they're still mired in their old ways, and it'll take time to drag them out.\r\n\r\nIn time, maybe we can turn this mud-filled little town into a new heart of the Saradominist faith- something with the right kind of smell.",
    "Goblin_B2": "23 Raktuber 4163\r\n\r\nGuthix forgive me, but I hate goblins. They’ve recently found their way to Ashenfall, and immediately started causing trouble. They’re strange little creatures. Green skin, powerful arms and an odour fouler than anything I’ve ever encountered. They seem to delight in nothing more than picking a fight with anything that moves. Or sometimes doesn’t move, I’ve seen them do battle with a rock.\r\n\r\nMostly I ignore them. They’ve tried to raid my hut a few times, but never in large numbers. I give them a sound thrashing with my broom and that’s normally enough to send them packing. They’re a pain more than anything, hardly a threat.\r\n\r\nThe threat is their god.\r\n\r\nI never met Guthix, I’m far too young, but I hear stories of how he towered above everyone and his presence made the air feel heavy. Their \"big high war god\" feels the same. Huge, hulking and layered in metal. A more brutal creature I dare not hope to meet. I dread the day that he decides to turn his ire on us, but thankfully his attention is focused elsewhere, on the beastmen of the wilds.\r\n\r\nGood, let him focus on them.",
    "DragonAttack_A2": "31 Raktuber 4213\r\n\r\nAs I write this, the villagers die around me. I cower beneath broken timber, hoping they do not hear the scratching of my quill against the page. I use my own blood as ink, like some infernal contract, but no matter how much I write prayers for salvation, no one hears my plea.\r\n\r\nIt was the beasts, the garou, who came for us, and they were not alone.\r\n\r\nI had thought them eradicated. The alliance with the war god and his foul-smelling minions, was so we could wipe out their moon goddess and cleanse the forests of their filth. We were so assured of our victory and we were so close to success.\r\n\r\nBut now, now their moon goddess rides atop a scaled nightmare. Flames for breath and swords for fangs. Beside her came two creatures I had never seen before. Scaled, winged, wicked, like the great beast the goddess rode. Around one was a halo of fire and the other was rimed with frost, scribbling a tally of our deaths in its journal.\r\n\r\nThey burned the city to the ground. Murdered the lord and his knights. We scattered into the woods, doomed.\r\n\r\nSaradomin, where are you?",
    "DragonAttack_A3": "4 Bennath 4210\r\n\r\nI sometimes find my thoughts wandering to home. I’ve been here for years, yet my heart will never belong here. It’s odd to long for a war-torn realm, a world where armies are on constant move and the threat of death greets you with a familiar smile each morning, like a bosom companion.\r\n\r\nThat’s home. War. A war raging for thousands of years. A war between the very gods themselves, a scale of destruction that must have been unthinkable before. Yet this is the only life I have known.\r\n\r\nWe’ve brought some of that war with us, of course. The high priest and the local lord have brokered an alliance of swords with Bandos’ goblins. Horrible little creatures, who want nothing but the thrill of slaughter. There is a shared enemy between us and we’ve agreed to wipe them out. The garou,  and their blasphemous goddess, they’ve overstayed their welcome.\r\n\r\nWe were here first, and we’ve no desire to share. Bandos wants revenge, for some slight or other the goddess created. We want to regain what is rightfully ours. So we’ll work together, and we’ll wipe those monsters out.\r\n\r\nThere can be no peace with animals.",
    "DragonAttack_A5": "A cold, dark day in the year 4267 of the third age, \r\n\r\nI am lost, and yet he does not look for me. I wait, oh, how I wait for you, oh Saradomin. I have been your faithful servant, and yet, here and now, where are you when I need you the most? \r\nThey’re dead. All of them. Everyone is gone. I hid beneath the rubble, trying to ignore the stench of their rotting bodies as I hid from the beasts. So much death, so much pain, and still, he does not come to save me. \r\n\r\nHave I sinned? Have I committed some hateful act that has offended you, oh great Saradomin? Is there any act of contrition that will save me from this endless nightmare?\r\n\r\nNo.\r\n\r\nNo, you were never that sort of god, were you? Only ever your glory, not ours. We’re nothing to you, are we? Just pawns in your games? Well, I refuse to play any longer. I spit on your name. I curse your countenance. I cry out into the dark that someone makes you suffer like you have left us to suffer. \r\n\r\nWhy did I ever think you could save us?\r\n\r\nCurse you, Saradomin.",
    "Guthix_C4_DisplayName": "Ancient Journal Page",
    "Garou_D5": "Before your grandfather had teeth, there was a king who was stronger than all his rivals.\r\n\r\nKing Rolthar was mighty, proud and gifted with cunning. Moon after moon, challengers would throw themselves at him, and each fell before the hour passed. He was beloved by his citizens, a wise king who kept our people strong.\r\n\r\nYet his strength was so great that none could match him, and it birthed a melancholy he could not escape. He sought foes that might prove a challenge. Seeking a victory worthy of praise.\r\n\r\nHe chose to face the dragon. Velgar was the strongest warrior in the realm. Rolthar spent months in preparation, crafted a blade of iron and sounded the challenge horn.\r\n\r\nThe dragon was too strong, his scales too solid, yet the king refused to relent. When Rolthar’s strength finally faltered, and his last breath escaped, he still held his blade.\r\n\r\nVelgar slew Rolthar, as all strongest must, and brought the body home. “This warrior is the pride of your people,” he told the tribe, “give him a burial worthy of his strength.” His resting place now sits high on the mountain, watching over us.\r\n\r\nRemember King Rolthar, little pups, for the worthy must never be forgotten.",
    "Goblin_B5": "Big high war god has left us. Big high war god ran away.\r\n\r\nBut you can’t run away, that illegal. Big high war god said so. What do we do when big high war god say one thing, then big high war god do another? I ask priest, priest said he a baker now – not a very good one, he burns the bread.\r\n\r\nAll priests very confused and argue over answer. We decide that since dragon won against the big high war god, then dragon must be stronger than big high war god. Which means now we worship dragon, because that’s how faith works.\r\n\r\nReligion very confusing, can see why priest become a baker even if priest can’t bake.\r\n\r\nGoing to workship dragon now, maybe he make us dragons too? I bet goblin dragons would be strongest dragons of all.\r\n\r\nVelgar is new big high war god. Glory be to Velgar.\r\n\r\nI hope new god isn’t hungry. ",
    "DragonAttack_A2_DisplayName": "Bloodstained Journal",
    "Abyssal_F1_DisplayName": "Bloodstained Page",
    "Dragonkin_E2_DisplayName": "Dragonkin Diary Page",
    "Dragonkin_E1_DisplayName": "Dragonkin Journal Page",
    "Dragonkin_E4_DisplayName": "Dragonkin Notebook Page",
    "Guthix_C2_DisplayName": "Druid's Memoirs",
    "CastleExtra_2_Name": "Duke's Diary",
    "DragonAttack_A1_DisplayName": "Dust-covered Diary",
    "Garou_D5_DisplayName": "Elder's Storybook Page",
    "Guthix_C3": "Even gods make mistakes, though his bring him laughter. Even as the lab explodes, Guthix’s latest experiment brings him almost child-like joy. \r\n\r\nWe pick ourselves up from the rubble and are met by mischievous giggles. There is a whimsiness in him that is usually crushed by a hidden melancholy, but now the mirth is on full display. \r\n\r\nAll over a rock. A piece of stone that he found hovering in the air as if it found gravity disdainful. He was fascinated immediately, sensing in it a potential our mortal gaze could not see. \r\n\r\nOver the months, he has poured into the stone what energies he can gather. Guthix believes that the elements themselves can be tamed within the rock. \r\n\r\nWe knew he was serious when he brought the great stone with him. Power radiates from it, and there’s a pressure to it like it’s the wall of a dam, and it’s about ready to burst. But it worked, and Guthix laughed with glee when he bound the very air itself into the rock. \r\n\r\nHe gave it to me, and I cast my first spell. A miracle in the palm of my hand.\r\n\r\nGlory to Guthix.",
    "Guthix_C5_DisplayName": "Forgotten Diary",
    "Garou_D2_DisplayName": "Garou Writings",
    "Goblin_B1_DisplayName": "Grimey Parchment",
    "Goblin_B2_DisplayName": "Grubby Note",
    "Goblin_B1": "Haha, I am writing on this paper thing, like a human. I am funny. Other goblins laugh. \r\n\r\nThis place is place for adventurers and heroes. Big shiny armour and swords that aren’t as rusted as they should be. Silly humans used to come here and pat each other on the back for not being eaten by a monster today. Then they would be sad when eaten by a monster tomorrow. \r\n\r\nThey all stupid. \r\n\r\nBest way to not be eaten by a monster, is to not be near a monster’s mouth. You run in the other direction, or you gang up on the monster with lots and lots of friends. If someone eaten, better chances it not you if there are lots of you. \r\n\r\nSee, goblins smart. Humans stupid. \r\n\r\nWriting stupid too. What is point of words on page, when words could be said out loud? \r\n\r\nHumans say pen mightier than sword, but I don’t think it would parry mine very well. \r\n\r\nMaybe it’s magic? I should test. I will ask Mucktooth to fight me with it. I bet he die.  \r\n\r\nHe died. \r\n\r\nPen is rubbish. Sword much better. ",
    "Dragonkin_E4": "I despise the rambling of seers. Viika persists with their inscrutable announcements of something sinister to come yet lacks the ability to make their meaning clear. Lacrussa fusses over their sibling as they have their little meltdown while irritating me with their lack of clarity. \r\n\r\nPrecision is important. Vagueness helps no one and causes more harm than good. Seers never understood this. I remember speaking to Kranon once, long before his fall, and he laughed with me about the eccentricities of the timeswept. He explained how they exist in moments of their lives other than the ones we are bound to, lost in eddies of temporal currents while the rest of us are anchored in place. \r\n\r\nIt seems like a cruel existence, to be certain, but that does not make up for the frustration they create. \r\n\r\nWhat do they mean when they say, “the blood makes her hunger”? What does that even mean? Who are these “warriors from across the sea” that will “put an end to her vengeance”. Who is “her”? Who are they? What in creation is the seer talking about?\r\n\r\nEnough. I’m done. I leave Lacrussa to her sibling’s nonsense. I have more pressing things to do. ",
    "Garou_D2": "I do not understand this concept of hate. The god of the greenskins feels it toward us with such a ferocity that you would think he was preparing for the hunt. I could respect that, but it isn’t his way. \r\n\r\nInstead of chasing us down or challenging our strongest, he sits in fortified battlements and sends an unending river of green-skinned warriors to smash against our defences. Even the smallest pup has slain a dozen of the vermin, yet their numbers seem almost endless, and there are always more to kill. \r\n\r\nThis relentless assault continues through the day and the night. As we rest, their sacrifice continues. As we tire, they gain ground. When we sleep, they push forward. We are losing this war, and it is not because of strength. \r\n\r\nI asked the goddess why they do this. What honour is there in such a shameful display? She says it is because he is jealous of us. Enraged by some slight we inflicted, some aeons ago, on a world far from here. \r\n\r\nHe hates with such fury that he would see his own people slaughtered just to wound us. A single drop of our blood, for oceans of theirs.",
    "DragonAttack_A4": "I don't remember the date, Fentuary maybe? 4265\r\n\r\nI know there’s no real reason to write this. No one’s going to read it. It’ll rot to nothing in time, even with the druid’s and their silly little rites. I think I’m just writing in this journal, because I want to take these memories out of my head and put them somewhere else. If I do that, maybe, just maybe, I can have one night’s sleep without hearing the screams.\r\n\r\nThe village is gone. Velgar, a great dragon, green as the grass, killed everyone who lived there. Nothing left but cinders and screaming spectres.\r\n\r\nThere was peace for a while, with the garou and their dragon army. We called a truce and the garou accepted, as long as we each kept to ourselves. For decades it held, and we almost forgot about battle, until we felt the ripple on the wind as a goddess died.\r\n\r\nThat’s when we knew that a new war was coming.\r\n\r\nNo, not a war. This was a massacre; we never stood a chance. Kuldra’s forces unleashed hate wreathed flames, and entire settlements vanished overnight. Goblin, human, gone in an instant.\r\n\r\nPerhaps we deserved it.",
    "Dragonkin_E1": "I have never understood my brethren’s calling to cower in the safety of dreams and let reality slip away. They choose to sleep, to pretend that our suffering does not exist. \r\n\r\nPathetic. \r\n\r\nWhile they tremble like hatchlings in the cold, I look to the future. This continent could be home to a kingdom. A new start, a new Orthen. One not chained down by the weakness and arrogance of our elders.  \r\n\r\nThe first, great, Dragonkin empire?\r\n\r\nThe stone here is sturdy; magical energies imbue it with a strength unlike any other on this pitiful planet. They can be tamed and shaped, even made to defy gravity itself. The magic Rasthin showed us is more than just power; it’s understanding. I listen to the stone, and I know how to shape it. It’s as simple as reaching down and telling it how it should be. \r\n\r\nNow, thanks to the aggressive natures of the lesser races, I have a workforce. The beastmen are stupid and easily distracted, but they are strong and know how to work. They are excellent tools, and I shall use them to craft a monument worthy of the name Brakka. ",
    "Guthix_C2": "I walk beside Guthix as we explore this strange land. We arrived on familiar green grass that echoed our homes, yet the more we explored, the stranger it became. There is an oddness to this continent, a sort of curse that changes things the deeper they get toward the centre. \r\n\r\nThere are wolves with manes made of leaves and deer with reed-like fronds as natural a part of them as their antlers. \r\n\r\nTrees, with leaves of shifted hues that emulate the sunset. Grass the colour of candlelight. \r\n\r\nIt’s as if Ashenfall takes something and twists it, infusing it with magic. Not destroying it, not even harming it, but making it different. Perhaps, in time, that might happen to us. I think I would suit a beard made of leaves. \r\n\r\nGuthix is fascinated, too, as much as a god can be. I see a smile on his face as he walks through the woods. It is as if he has discovered the beginning threads of a secret, and he seeks to unravel the knots. \r\nI look forward to the revelations to come. ",
    "Dragonkin_E3_DisplayName": "Infused Journal",
    "Garou_D3": "Ire Of Phyrrys 4213\r\n\r\nThe beastman and their goddess no longer stand alone. Our alliance forced them back into the shadows, and we were so close to removing their stain from this sacred land. Yet, somehow, they have plucked new friends from the shadows. Allies of a terrible power that we had no inkling of before. \r\n\r\nThe dragons they summon are terror enough. Setting fire to our villages, burning our watchtowers to ash. This would be dangerous enough, yet the four commanders scare me the most. \r\n\r\nThey are smaller than the dragons but bear their features. Great leathery wings and glistening scales. They wield frightening magic that decimates battalions, and they do so with the cold impartiality of the rat catcher. \r\n\r\nIn their eyes, we are nothing but vermin, and they treat us appropriately. \r\n\r\nNot all are killed; some are taken. Dragged into great vaults filled with nothing but screams. I hear rumours of cruel experiments and sick entertainment. Yet most of us are nought but food for their beasts. \r\n\r\nIs this some malicious form of justice? Were we wrong to betray the beastmen when we did?\r\n\r\nSaradomin save us. Nothing else will. ",
    "Abyssal_F2_DisplayName": "Leaf-scented Page",
    "Garou_D4_DisplayName": "Leathery Parchment",
    "Goblin_B5_DisplayName": "Muddy Scrawl",
    "Garou_D4": "My people have a tradition that is sacred above all others; the right of challenge. There is nothing we respect more than strength or cunning. When one defeats a challenger, they prove themselves rightful of their position. When one fails, they prove themselves inadequate. \r\n\r\nEven gods must acknowledge this truth. \r\n\r\nThe High Queen, lady Lougrim, earned her place by challenging the kings of old. Taking on all of them in one mythical battle and emerging the victor. In the centuries that have followed, she has held her position and bested all challengers that think themselves her rival. \r\n\r\nThat winning streak ended today when the dragon queen took the throne. \r\n\r\nThe battle was swift and bloody; their clashing energies created cracks in the very earth. The entire continent buckled beneath their fury, but only one of them could prevail. Her many heads tore the goddess limb from limb, swallowing down the pieces of her divine flesh until nothing of the old queen remained. \r\n\r\nNow we have a new queen, and long may she reign. \r\n\r\nHail to High Queen Kuldra, the god eater. ",
    "Abyssal_F1": "My wound is a lethal one, so I leave this message as a last letter to my siblings in arms. \r\n\r\nI am proud to be one of the Wild Knights, chosen by Guthix to defend people from nature and nature from people. I am a guardian between two worlds, and it fills me with pride. But what I encountered just a few days prior was not from either world. \r\n\r\nIt was a monster. A demon. Blade-like talons where arms should be, and it arrived in a flash of purple lightning. Its chitinous hide repelled my blade, and my spells caused no sign of flinching. I found it in the fog as I wandered that poisonous swamp searching for a fugitive. I found the criminal; just as his bloodied torso slipped into that wicked maw. \r\n\r\nThe universe has its own sense of justice. \r\n\r\nIf it hadn’t fed, I am sure I wouldn’t be here. It was sated, slower than it could have been, giving me a chance. Barely. It plunged one of those wicked pincers through my stomach, and I narrowly escaped with my life. \r\n\r\nWhat’s left of it. \r\n\r\nI pray my siblings do not find it.",
    "CastleExtra_1": "No one in the castle knows what I am. They barely know who I am. I walk these walls as a shadow, forgotten and unseen by all who dwell within. Priests, nobles, and gurning knights, none of them know that I am a Child of Darkness, a servant of shadows within the Duke’s court.\r\n\r\nI could bring death. I could bring chaos. I could bring pain to them all. With a few carefully chosen words, or some redistributed wealth, it would be oh so simple for me to bring these Saradominist fools to their knees.\r\n\r\nI wash their socks. I bring their meals. I spit in their mugs before bringing them breakfast. All that while I stand beside them as the architect of their future downfall.\r\n\r\nThere’s another meeting of the Children of Shadows soon. Apparently, there are rumours of secret structures, buried under the ground and the other Children believe that they might contain something we could use to remake this sad, pathetic world. A weapon, perhaps. New magic to wield. Some dread, and deadly monster we could unleash upon these fools.\r\n\r\nSo, yes, my Duke, I’ll bring you your socks, and your drinks, and your scones. But mark my word, I’ll bring you your end soon enough.\r\n\r\nHail Zamorak!",
    "Guthix_C1_DisplayName": "Preserved Diary",
    "DragonAttack_A3_DisplayName": "Priest's Journal",
    "Goblin_B4_DisplayName": "Pungent Scribble",
    "Garou_D1": "Raktuber 1466\r\n\r\nThey came in the night. The driver fell first; his life quickly ended with an arrow to the neck. Eva grabbed her staff and prepared to unleash a torrent of flame on our attackers, but a crack of thunder sent us sprawling across the forest floor. \r\n\r\nEric vanished, yelping as something dragged him into the tree line. Only for the scream to silence suddenly with terrifying finality.\r\n\r\nI readied my bow as Eva hurled flames into the woods and, in the flickering lights as her fire blast dwindled, I caught sight of yellow eyes glinting in the darkness. Pure evil.\r\n\r\nThey charged, sweeping out of the forests like shadows with teeth. \r\n\r\nLike wolves that walk on two legs, almost human in their stance, but in the short-lived embers of Eva’s magic, I saw no sign of humanity – only malice. They ran at us with saliva dripping from elongated fangs and claws that glinted unpleasantly in the moonlight. \r\n\r\nI felled two of them with my arrows before they caught up to Eva and turned the evening’s rain a horrible shade of scarlet. \r\n\r\nI ran, and they let me escape. \r\n\r\nThey’re toying with me. \r\n\r\nI can’t run far enough.",
    "Garou_D3_DisplayName": "Scorched Journal",
    "DragonAttack_A4_DisplayName": "Scrawled Diary Page",
    "CastleExtra_1_Name": "Servant's Secret Diary",
    "Guthix_C3_DisplayName": "Soot-stained Diary",
    "DragonAttack_A5_DisplayName": "Tear-stained journal",
    "Goblin_B4": "That weren’t meant to happen.\r\n\r\nIt were meant to be lots of us and lots of the humans, and then we were meant to skewer the beastmen on the end of our spears. Big high war god was gonna be real pleased with us all, and then we were gonna have a feast.\r\n\r\nInstead we’re the feast!\r\n\r\nThat’s not fair. That’s not how it meant to work.\r\n\r\nThere I was, chasing down a beastman runt, when a great walloping dragon comes outa nowhere and lands on the goblin boss man. Squashes him into jelly, and not the good kind with bits of fruit – the bad kind, with bits of chieftain. Then, dragon goes for the rest of us, breathes a great big jet of fire which turns all of me friends into charcoal.\r\n\r\nWhen did dragons work with beastmen?\r\n\r\nWhy did dragons work with beastmen?\r\n\r\nWhat did dragons? Huh?\r\n\r\nThinking make my head hurt.\r\n\r\nSod this, I’m gonna go hide in a cave til it all goes away. Goblins good at hiding in caves. Probably nothing bad in caves.",
    "CastleExtra_2": "The priests are very helpful, always offering advice, always steering me in the right direction. I was wavering over how to handle the old Guthixian followers, you know, those weird people in the leaf covered rags, and the priests gave me the most helpful advice.\r\n\r\nJust send them away.\r\n\r\nSo simple really, why didn’t I think of it. After all, those druids so love the forests, the woods and those weird, damp, little caves, that they’d be delighted at the chance to go and move into them. No longer frustrated by the noise of progress, they could return to their quiet contemplations about squirrels and twigs.\r\n\r\nI assume that’s what they do.\r\n\r\nThe priests are so wise. I mean they must be to put my family in charge of this place. We were once simple officials, but now look at us, the Dukes of Brynmoor. Noble rulers of all, just as we deserve to be.\r\n\r\nThey’re coming over to talk with me later, something to do with our little Garou problem. I’m sure they will have most delightful solution to the situation. I would very much like to expand our little kingdom into Ghornfel. Pink is my favourite colour, after all.",
    "Guthix_C1": "Today, I summoned a miracle. Thanks to these new stones, gifts from the great Guthix himself, I have performed a spell warding wood from rot. My hut, simple as it is, will now stand the test of time for generations to come. Even this journal and these silly words on paper will stand unsullied for aeons to pass. That such wonders are so commonplace is truly a miracle. \r\n\r\nGlory be to Guthix.   \r\n\r\nHe calls these stones “Runes”. Within each of them is an element imprisoned and waiting to be unleashed. The more complex the combination of runes, the more intricate the spell, and the more we learn about them, the more fantastic our workings. \r\n\r\nOvernight, our world has changed. We no longer use flint for fire when a snap of our fingers serves the same effect. The air can be used as a blade that makes wheat harvests easy. It is the dawn of a miraculous new era where we can make a better world. \r\n\r\nThis new continent must be so full of wonders if it has led our lord to create these marvels.",
    "Garou_D1_DisplayName": "Torn Journal Page",
    "Abyssal_F2": "We Wild Knights rarely gather. We spend so much time alone, wandering the wildlands, that we can go weeks, sometimes months, before speaking to another person. This can stunt our conversation, or sometimes the inverse. \r\n\r\nAidan is the talkative kind. He turns solitude into a gaseous buildup that he belches upon each of us as an endless stream of words. Every thought, feeling, and tiny observation is unleashed upon the rest of us the moment we meet. \r\n\r\nBut today, there is silence, and I find I miss the noise. \r\n\r\nAidan died valiantly defending his brothers. A group of them went out in search of some beast—some foul, fetid creature in the poisonous fog. It’s clear that they found it and that it led to his death. His brothers mourn him silently; they’re alive because he isn’t. \r\n\r\nI think he would prefer to be mourned in sound. \r\n\r\nLamented with cacophony, a wake of jeering shouts, one night of endless chitchat in memory of him. A brother lost, a brother remembered. Two left who’ll carry his name, as is tradition. \r\n\r\nHe died to save them, so they now proudly bear his name. ",
    "Dragonkin_E2": "We are finally free from our kin’s grasp. They can no longer hunt us down, searching for Lacrussa’s accursed sibling. To know the future and yet not offer us guidance, what is the point of a seer that does not see? \r\n\r\nRasthin urges patience, Avisk calls for calm, and Lacrussa ignores us, content to have her family returned to her. All of us stand in defiance of our kin’s traditions. We forged our own path and found somewhere new. \r\n\r\nThis continent is remarkable. It is flush with energy that seeps into the stone, the trees, the water, and even the air, and it feels alive with possibility. The creatures here are transformed, taking on aspects both elemental and primal. What wonderful possibilities this place offers. \r\n\r\nI can do a lot with this continent. The stone looks sturdy, the metal firm. Even the wood feels as though I could make it last centuries before it rots into nothing. It is the perfect place to create a new home. To fashion the foundations of the next dragonkin city. \r\n\r\nViika whispers that the structures will last. Dragonkin towers standing against the flow of time.  \r\n\r\nMonuments to my genius. ",
    "Guthix_C4": "We are lost without him, though we pretend otherwise. The absence of his divine presence is felt through every household. We pray, follow the rituals, and live our lives as best we can, but it is not the same. \r\n\r\nWas he right to be angry? Lives were lost after all. So many dead, far too many, and we justified it because we told ourselves that they were no longer human. They were Amalgamated. They were impure, imperfect -- wrong. \r\n\r\nOur hatred must have been like poison to him. To see this tranquil home we had created fall to bitter infighting and needless hate. For there is nothing so human as to despise. \r\n\r\nHe left. Took some of the faithful with him, those who had not fallen to our cruel prejudices. In his last moments, he tasked the Wild Knights to uphold their oaths, protecting both us from the wild and the wild from us, and then he left. \r\n\r\nThe captain of the Knights took some of the abandoned children under her wing. Those whose parents were lost to our venom. It will be a hard life, but better than they’ll have here. \r\n\r\nWe are such fools.",
    "Guthix_C5": "We have fallen so far as to go from god to godless. Worse still, to have the vile beastmen parade their own deity in front of us as though we’re unworthy of divine consideration. \r\n\r\nShe is beautiful and alien like all such beings are. Her words are soft and gentle, though the barbs are barely hidden. Her presence is a statement that any harm to her people will be met with swift retribution, and we lack the power to stand up to a god. \r\n\r\nWe’ve managed without Guthix’s presence for centuries now. It should be easy. Yet, when I see her moonlit figure glide through our village as she and the chieftain meet for diplomatic conversation, I can’t help the envy that stirs in my gut. A green-eyed worm writhing in jealousy. \r\n\r\nWe were abandoned. They were not. Aren’t we more deserving than the beasts?\r\n\r\nI pray that we are found worthy again. That a god reaches their gaze toward us and recognizes what we’ve created. Ashenfall deserves to be a human nation. \r\n\r\nI refuse to let it fall to animals.",
    "Dragonkin_E3": "We used to talk about power as if it were some ephemeral notion—a collection of things—status, skill, charisma, all stacked together in one umbrella term. But that’s not real power; this is. What now courses through my veins is the embodiment of that word. In me is the very essence of the stone itself. \r\n\r\nNot just the stone but the earth, the dirt, and the plants that grow within it. I feel each of them, and with a wave of my hand, I make them follow my will. \r\n\r\nIs this what it feels like to be a god? To command dominion over elemental earth? It moves as I beckon; it shapes as I command. With a thought, I conjure a tower that would have taken me months to craft before. \r\n\r\nKerapac was a fool to seek the Anathema. The real power is here, in this place. The discarded afterthoughts of the Elder God’s dinner, but in our hands, it’s a magic without equal. \r\n\r\nAnd they do not stir in response. They slumber still, ignoring our ascension. \r\n\r\nViika was right. This place is special. Yet they choose not to claim the gift. Why? I wonder. ",
    "Goblin_B3_DisplayName": "Weathered Diary"
  },
  "NewStringTable": {
    "Loadstone.FastTravelCost": "Cost:",
    "Legend.Header": "Legend",
    "Marker.MapMarker": "Map Marker",
    "Message.WaitingForView": "Minimap waiting for MapView",
    "Quests.PrimaryQuestCategory": "Primary Quests",
    "Quests.SecondaryQuestCategory": "Secondary Quests"
  },
  "Notification": {
    "RemainingBuildingProtectionTotems": "Totems available: {0}"
  },
  "PauseMenu": {
    "ServerName": "Server name: {0}"
  },
  "QF_Doric_Dialogue": {
    "Statue_GraniteMaul_LastStatue": "A seal somewhere has broken. ",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_GotBlueprint_Intro4": "Ah, enjoy making that. These sorts of weapons are what an artisan lives for.",
    "Objective2_KnowDoric": "Bring the blueprint to Doric in Ashien's Watch.",
    "Objective2_DontKnowDoric": "Find someone near Ashien's Watch that can translate ancient dwarvish. ",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Started_NoBlueprint1": "How's the investigation going? I know Ashien's Watch must have something interesting to discover.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_GotBlueprint_Intro3": "Hrmm, this looks like a blueprint for a very special weapon, and look, I already found a bit to get you started!",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_NoBlueprint_Intro3": "I found a strange stone block covered in weird sigils, but then the garou ran me out of the place with threats of pointy sticks.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_NoBlueprint_Intro4": "I'm guessing you're much better at all this fighting malarky. Mind poking around? See what's sealed away?",
    "Objective1": "Investigate the secrets hidden below Ashien's Watch.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_NoBlueprint_Intro2": "It's the sort of place where dragonkin would have hoarded their more interesting stuff. Feels like the sort of thing they'd do.",
    "Doric_GraniteMauled_Generic_FirstTime_Intro": "Oh, hello again. I'm impressed you've made it all the way out here. Really coming into your own, eh?",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Started_GotBlueprint1": "Oh, what's that? You found something? Let me take a look at that blueprint for you.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_GotBlueprint_Intro2": "Oh, you've already been in the vault? Brilliant, what did you find?",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Started_GotBlueprint_DoesNotHaveSpace": "Oh. You appear to be a little overburdened. I've got something for you, but you should come back to me when you have space to carry it. ",
    "VaultDoor_GraniteMaul_Locked": "The door is sealed by Dragonkin magic.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Complete": "The granite maul, now there's a weapon with heft. I wonder what other wonders the vaults are hiding?",
    "VaultStatue_GraniteMaul_GotBlueprint": "The statue has no further secrets for you.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Started_GotBlueprint_HasSpace": "These sorts of weapons are what an artisan lives for. Enjoy crafting it and then hitting your enemies with it.",
    "Description": "Uncover the secrets of Ashien's Watch.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_Started_GotBlueprint2": "Well now, that explains this great hunk o' stone, it's the head to a great ruddy weapon. Here, I think I know how to make it now.",
    "VaultStatue_GraniteMaul_QuestStarted_NotGotBlueprint": "You find a weapon blueprint written in dwarvish. Perhaps Doric can help translate it.",
    "VaultStatue_GraniteMaul_QuestNotStarted_NotGotBlueprint": "You find a weapon blueprint written in dwarvish. Perhaps someone nearby can help translate it.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_GotBlueprint_Intro1": "You see that place over there? Ashien's Watch they calls it. Used to be a site of some battle or other.",
    "Doric_GraniteMaul_NotStarted_NoBlueprint_Intro1": "You see that place over there? Ashien's Watch they calls it. Used to be a site of some battle or other."
  },
  "QF_FTUE_Dialogue": {
    "FTUE_Zanik_Spells3": " Ashenfall is rife with magic, and spells will come easy to you as you improve your skills. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Dodge1": " Dodging away from an enemy will stop them landing that killing blow. Time it right, then roll out of the way just before the enemy strikes.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Dodge2": " and you'll find yourself able to overcome almost any foe. ",
    "FTUE_Doric_Intro3": "A new continent, hidden for centuries by Guthix's magic. I mean, would could turn down a chance to explore that?",
    "Doric_RightTool_Intro_1": "Ah, the new recuit, pleasure to meet you. I'm Doric, smith and general handydwarf of this humble expedition.",
    "FTUE_Doric_Intro1": "Aha, the new recruit, great to see you. Heard the call of adventure  and just couldn't resist?",
    "FTUE_VannakaCombatLink": "Alright, what do you need help with?",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_SpokenTo_NotGotGear2": "Any piece will do, but consider a full set. You need to keep yourself properly protected.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_hub": "Anything I can help with?",
    "WoM_Tutorial_GenericNotFinishedText": "Aren't you helping the others out? What are you talking to me for? Check your map if you're not sure what you're meant to be doing.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_CraftThings1": "As you collect materials, you'll think up new ways to use them. These recipes can then be created using the right workstations. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Spells1": "As you improve your abilities you'll discover spells that will prove themselves quite useful.",
    "Doric_Generic_TutorialInProgress_Text": "Ashenfall is a dangerous place, but one full of opportunity. Make sure you take the time to explore it properly.",
    "FTUE_Doric_Intro5": "Ashenfall is full of secrets, if you find any interesting blueprints or anything, come find me.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_NotBuiltBed2": "Ashenfall's a harsh place to live in, you're gonna need a shelter and somewhere to rest.",
    "PlayerChoice_AbyssalWhipped": "Ask about Abyssal Whipped.",
    "PlayerChoice_AboutDogDogs": "Ask about Dog Days.",
    "PlayerChoice_GoblinDiplomacy": "Ask about Goblin Diplomacy",
    "PlayerChoice_GraniteMauled": "Ask about Granite Mauled.",
    "Doric_RightTool_SpokenTo_MadeAxe_1": "Aye, that's a fine axe you got there, but even the best tools break over time. When that happens use a crafting bench to repair your gear.",
    "Vannaka_PostQuest": "Be sure to keep your armour and weapons in a good state of repair. I've lost too many friends to lazy maintenance. ",
    "FirstSteps_Desc": "Begin your adventure. ",
    "Butterknife_Title": "Better than a butterknife",
    "Doric_RightTool_Intro_4": "Both require stone and ash logs, which you'll find scattered all over the ground around here.",
    "Objective_Ratcatcher_1": "Bring 3 small animal fangs to Vannaka",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Cook1": "Build a campfire, using ash logs and stone. Keep the fire burning with a fuel source, such as ash logs.",
    "Objective_SeekingShelter_1": "Build and then claim a bed. ",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_3": "But before all that, how about we take you through some survival basics?",
    "PlayerChoice_CombatTips": "Can you give me any combat tips?",
    "PlayerChoice_Spells": "Can you tell me about skilling spells?",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_NotGotGear4": "Come see me wearing a piece set of good quality armour and I'll know you're ready.",
    "RightTool_Objective_1": "Craft a stone logging axe at a workbench and show it to Doric. ",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_SpokeToBefore_BuiltBed2": "Death's made a deal with the Wise Old Coot, so if you die you'll just find yourself in your bed again. Handy right?",
    "FTUE_Zanik_WhoAreYou3": "Don't recommend the dying bit. I had some special circumstances that brought me back. Not something to chat about now. But, the rest of the stuff, crafting, building, survival tips – I'm your gal. ",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokeTo_GotFangs2": "Don't worry, you can keep them. Turn them into something useful.",
    "RightTool_Desc": "Doric wants to teach you the fundamentals. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_AboutExpedition2": "Exploration always draws excitement, and there's a mad rush to be the first people to claim the resources of an undiscovered land. So this expedition was quickly put together by interested investors, and then the first wave of explorers set off to sites unknown.",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_SkipTutorial_1": "Fair enough, I do like someone that can show initiative.",
    "FirstSteps_name": "First Steps",
    "FTUE_Zanik_BuildThings4": "For a complete shelter, you'll need a roof over your head, to keep the rain off you at night. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Block1": "Get a hunk of wood or metal between yourself and the attack. Blocking is tiring though, it'll drain yer stamina, so try and time it for maximum effect. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_ImproveHealth1": "Get yourself a good meal in you, that'll give you the energy you need to get going. Start with berries you forage, but there's better food around. Food will generally need to be cooked on a campfire before its edible. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Intro_FirstTime2": "Get yourself some decent gear. A butter-knife won't do you any good in a place like this. ",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_IgnoredWoM1": "Getting ahead of yourself aren't you? You see the old-geezer with the beard, back in the temple? That's the Wise Old Man, the boss of this expedition.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_NotGotFangs5": "Giant rats can be found all over this region, but the windmill, behind me, is infested with them. I'd start there if I were you.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_NotGotGear3": "Go and craft yourself better gear. Warrior, mage, ranger, whatever combat style you like, but I want to see better quality than what you're wearing now.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_IgnoredWoM2": "Go introduce yourself before he gets cranky. You won't like him when he's cranky.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Hello": "Hail adventurer, anything I can help with?",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokenTo_NotGotFangs3": "Happy hunting.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_CraftThings4": "Have a go at something simple, you'll soon get the hang of it. ",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_AcceptTutorial_3": "He's the only dwarf on the continent, that we know of anyway, can't miss him.",
    "FTUE_WoM_Intro_DragonSlayerSet": "Hello, adventurer. Don't you have a dragon to kill? Or is there something you needed?",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_CompleteQuest1": "Here, something to help you in your adventures.",
    "Doric_RightTool_SpokenTo_MadeAxe_2": "Here, something to reward your effort.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_CompleteQuest_GotSpace": "Here, this'll help you on your journey. Now, get out there and make the beasts of Ashenfall regret your arrival.",
    "Zanik_prequest_generic": "Hi there. It's good to see new blood, hope you're ready to brave this place. I think Doric needs your attention, best say hi. ",
    "PlayerChoice_Avoid": "How can I avoid battle?",
    "PlayerChoice_Block": "How do I block?",
    "PlayerChoice_BuildThings": "How do I build things?",
    "PlayerChoice_Cook": "How do I cook raw food?",
    "PlayerChoice_Craft": "How do I craft things?",
    "PlayerChoice_Cold": "How do I deal with the cold?",
    "PlayerChoice_Dodge": "How do I dodge?",
    "PlayerChoice_HowDoIImproveHealth": "How do I improve my health and stamina?",
    "PlayerChoice_Parry": "How do I parry?",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Sneak2": "However, if you need to get past them, then stealth is your friend. Keep low, move slowly and you might avoid their attention. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Intro_FirstTime1": "Hrmm, let's take a look at you. Aye, I can see it, that look in your eyes. That twitch at the end of your fingers. Your a warrior, well and proper. Good we need someone like that here. This place is dangerous, like a wild animal, and it'll tear you apart without a moment's hesitation.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_CompleteQuest_NotGotSpace": "Hrmm, you appear to be overburdened. Come back to me when you have space free for your reward. ",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_NotGotGear1": "I already lost one young warrior to the dangers of this place, I refuse to lose another.",
    "PlayerChoice_FirstSteps_SkipTutorial": "I can work it out [Skip Tutorial]",
    "FTUE_Doric_Intro2": "I don't blame you. I'm the same. Found myself here after too many pints at the Blue Moon Inn.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_SpokenTo_NotGotGear1": "I don't care what style you choose, but I want to see you wearing armour that's at least good enough to face a goblin.",
    "PlayerChoice_BuildAndCraft": "I have some questions about building and crafting. ",
    "PlayerChoice_Survival": "I have some questions about survival techniques.",
    "Zanik_RuneMysteries_Intro_1": "I imagine you've been seeing your skills grow stronger. As you level up, you'll unlock special spells to make surviving here easier.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_NotGotFangs3": "I need three animal fangs. You can get them from killing giant rats. Nasty little critters, more dangerous than kebbits that's for sure.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_WhoAreYou1": "I see we Slayer Masters aren't quite as famous as we like to think we are then. Haha, that's for the best, I think. Fame distracts us from the thrill of combat, and a warrior must always be ready to hone their art. ",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_SpokeToBefore_BuiltBed1": "I see you've got yourself all set up now, great work!",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou3": "I used to be an adventurer, like you. My exploits took me across all of Gielinor, where I battled evil, slew monsters and ended wars. It was a hard life, but morally rewarding.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_BuiltBed1": "I was going to get you started by tasking you with making a shelter and claiming yourself a bed for the night, but it looks like you're way ahead of me.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_GotFangs1": "I was going to see if you had what it takes to survive this gods forsaken land, but it looks like you beat me to it. Vicious little critters those rats eh?",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_GotGear1": "I was going to task you with getting some better equipment, but it appears you don't need that particular lesson.",
    "Doric_RightTool_Intro_2": "I won't beat around the bush, it's all hands on deck here and right now you're just not equipped for the job.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_WhoAreYou5": "I'll be heading out north, deeper into the wild lands. Got my eye on something pers... on some legends I've been hearing. Say hi if you see me. ",
    "PlayerChoice_HerdRing": "I'll take the Ring of the Herd.",
    "PlayerChoice_HermitRing": "I'll take the Ring of the Hermit. ",
    "FTUE_Doric_QuestLink": "I'm not really set up to look into those here. I've got all me notes up north in Ghornfell. Come find me out there and I can look into that for you. ",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Complete": "If you're after any more survival tips, I'm your gal. If you're looking for some fighting advice, you can find Vannaka just down the road. He'll get you sorted. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Parry2": "If you've got the timing down, you should be able to turn the force of their attack back against them.",
    "FTUE_WoM_AboutExpedition1": "It was a few months back when the continent was first discovered.  Someone bumped into it, literally, with their boat – the entire place is hidden behind a veil. A whopping great landmass that had been completely unheard of except for a few obscure texts.",
    "RuneMysteries_Desc": "Learn the basics of crafting runes. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_DragonSlayerLink": "Let's see...",
    "FTUE_Zanik_WhoAreYou2": "Like you, I'm here seeking the thrill of adventure. I've done some exploring in my time. First of my people to visit the surface. One of the first people to visit the husk of the goblin homeworld, Yu'Biusk. Died a couple of times, so I know a thing or two about survival. ",
    "Doric_RightTool_Intro_GotAxe_1": "Looks like you've already got to grips with crafting tools and weapons, so here's a little something to help you on your way.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_NotBuiltBed3": "Make yourself a shelter out of wood and stone. Any building will do, just needs floors, walls and a roof. When building, be sure to keep your structure stable. ",
    "RuneMysteries_Objective_2": "Mine rune essence, build a rune altar and craft some air runes.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokeTo_GotFangs3": "Most enemies are more dangerous than rats. Keep an eye out on what an opponent is resistant to and choose your style to counter it.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_SpokenTo_GotGear1": "Much better! You're all ready to face the dangers ahead.",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou2": "My name is Dionysius, but most people just call me the Wise Old Man. Or 'Ultraviolet Archangel Threat' when they think I'm not listening.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_SpokeToBefore_QuestNotComplete": "Not finished yet? Once you've made a shelter, make sure you've claimed a bed. Then come back and see me.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Started_NotComplete_1": "Not made any runes yet? It's quite simple really, you just need to find a source of rune essence.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_WhoAreYou3": "Now I'm here. Because... because there's more evil. There's more danger. But there's... no, never mind. Not important. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_AboutExpedition5": "Now that we know the first lot were all murdered by dragons, goblins and some aggressively fuzzy locals, we can start to push forward and do a better job of exploring. And by we, I mean you. I'm going to have a nice cup of tea and wait until you report back. Have fun. ",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_NotGotFangs2": "Now then, let's see if you've got what it takes to survive in this gods forsaken land.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_CompleteQuest": "Now, all the fashionable people accessorise, so here's a couple of rings to choose from.",
    "Doric_RightTool_SpokenTo_MadeAxe_3": "Now, go chat with Zanik next, the friendly little green lass on the other side of the path by that tent. She'll teach you how to build a shelter.",
    "WoM_LinkToRatcatcher_1": "Now, onto the scary stuff. You'll want to talk to Vannaka next. He'll help you avoid a brutal and agonising death...maybe. Have fun!",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_SkipTutorial_2": "Now, tell me, how do you feel about slaying dragons?",
    "Vannaka_Butterknife_LinkToWom": "Now, young pup, your real adventure begins. Go and speak to the Wise Old Man again, he'll get you up to speed. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_QuestLink_Goblins": "Oh, hey. Look, if you want to talk about goblins, let's do it away from here. Some of the others can get a bit jumpy and I'd prefer to keep it between us. Meet me back near the castle and we can go over it. ",
    "FTUE_Doric_WhoAreYou1": "Oh, sorry, didn't introduce myself. Names Doric, dwarven master crafstman and retired warrior.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Parry1": "Parrying an attack is all about timing. Wait for the right moment, just as the enemy is about to land their strike, and then block the attack.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Cook2": "Put your raw food on the campfire and wait for it to cook. Then, voila, you'll have a tasty meal.",
    "Ratcatcher_Title": "Ratcatcher",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou1": "Really? You haven't heard of me? Oh how marvelously refreshing. So often people are all; 'oh my hero', 'please name my baby for me', or 'aaargh no, please don't burn me to ash'. The usual. ",
    "RightTool_Objective_2": "Return to Doric and show him the stone logging axe. ",
    "RightTool_name": "Right Tool for the Job",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_GiveReward": "Right, now on to the next part of your survival training.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Sneak1": "Run away, haha. That's the easiest way to avoid battle. If you see an enemy you're not ready to fight, don't fight them. Just get out of there. ",
    "RuneMysteries_Name": "Rune Mysteries",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Intro_2": "Runes are made from rune essence, a special kind of stone that absorbs and holds magical power - anima.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Intro_MadeRunes_1": "Runes, I was all set to explain them, but it looks like you've already worked it out. Good job!",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Intro_1": "Runes, right? Thousands of years ago Guthix created special stones containing magical power. Runes.",
    "SeekingShelter_Title": "Seeking Shelter",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Cold2": "Shelter is also important, as when you're away from the elements, it's easier to keep warm and dry.",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_QuestLink": "Shh, not here. This isn't the place for that sort of conversation. Prying eyes and nosey gods listening in on their temples. Come talk to me up in Ghornfell, we can speak there. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou5": "So I took what was owed me. Walked into a bank, got myself nicely set up and acquired this rather fetching hat. After all, the bank didn't do anything to protect the world and without me there'd be no bank at all. So fairs fair. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Cold3": "Some clothing will also help to keep the cold at bay, so make sure you're always in the best gear you can be. ",
    "FirstSteps_Objective2": "Speak to Doric outside the Temple.",
    "Objective_ButterKnife_1": "Speak to Vannaka while wearing a piece of armour of power level 2 or higher.",
    "Ratcatcher_Objective_1": "Speak to Vannaka.",
    "Objective_SeekingShelter_2": "Speak to Zanik.",
    "FirstSteps_Objective1": "Speak to the Wise Old Man in the Temple.",
    "RuneMysteries_Objective_1": "Speak to the Wise Old Man in the temple.",
    "RuneMysteries_Objective_3": "Speak to the Wise Old Man in the temple.",
    "Objective_ButterKnife_2": "Speak to the Wise Old Man in the temple. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_BuildThings3": "Start with floors, and then build the walls on those. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_CraftThings2": "Take a look around and pick up some stones and ash logs. You'll then be able to combine them at a craftstation to create an axe, which will make cutting down trees much easier. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_ImproveHealth4": "The boosts a good meal gives you won't last forever, so keep an eye on how full your feeling and make sure to keep a good snack on hand when you're exploring.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Cold1": "The easiest way to deal with the cold, is to make yourself warm and comfortable by the fire. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_CraftThings3": "The more materials you find, the more recipes you'll discover. ",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_WhoAreYou2": "The names Vannaka, I'm a Slayer Master and mentor to new warriors, like yourself. I've trained scores of wannabe heroes, and I've slain my fair share of big and nasty types. I've walked the forests of Gielinor, sword in hand, and defeated ancient evils that would have swallowed the world whole.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokenTo_NotGotFangs2": "The windmill behind me is infested with the beasts, you may want to look there to gather the fangs.",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_NotBuiltBed4": "Then make and claim a bed to rest in. To make a bed you're going to need something soft, like fur. Look around for small creatures to get fur from.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_ImproveHealth2": "There are lots of ways you can prepare delicious meals on Ashenfall, each will help make your exploration easier.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Intro_3": "There's a deposit of essence behind this temple. Go mine it, then build yourself a rune altar. You might want to get yourself a pickaxe.",
    "FTUE_Doric_Intro4": "There's a few of us, though less than there were. Some stuff happened, but the Wise Old Man over there can fill you in.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_CompleteQuest2": "They're magic, so pick carefully. If you hunt alone, you'll want the ring of the hermit, if not go with the herd.",
    "FTUE_Doric_Secrets2": "This whole continent has been magically hidden for thousands of years. There's got to be interesting mysteries buried about the place.",
    "Zanik_RuneMysteries_Intro_2": "To cast spells you're going to need to learn about runes. The Wise Old Man can help you with that.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Spells2": "To cast these spells, you'll need runes, which you can craft by harvesting rune essence – those floating rocks over yonder.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_ImproveHealth3": "Try combining different meals, for a nutritious balanced diet. ",
    "Butterknife_Description": "Vannaka wants prove you're well equipped for future conflict. ",
    "Ratcatcher_Description": "Vannaka wants you to prove yourself in combat. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_AboutExpedition3": "We haven't heard from any of them. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_AboutExpedition4": "We're wave two. They went with more seasoned adventurers, like myself, as well as the expenda... the enthusiastic up-and-comers, like yourself. ",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_1": "Welcome to Ashenfall, sorry about the mess. Had a bit of a dragon problem, that's why we've called for you.",
    "Vannaka_prequest_generic": "Welcome to Ashenfall, young pup. Others got you all working away? Come chat to me when you're a little less busy. ",
    "FTUE_Doric_Secrets1": "Well if I knew, then they wouldn't be secrets, would they?",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Intro": "Well met adventurer. What do you need?",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_NotGotFangs1": "Well met, young pup. Fresh off the lodestone and raring for adventure? Good, good, that's what I like to hear.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokenTo_NotGotFangs1": "Well met, young pup. Seems like you haven't managed to gather three animal fangs for me yet. You can get them from the giant rats around this region.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_SpokeTo_GotFangs1": "Well met, young pup. Seems your hunt was successful, I see you've gathered the fangs I asked for.",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou4": "Well morally rewarding wasn't as much fun as one would hope. Oh, sure, people were friendly. Everyone waved. But when you've saved the world several times, it just feels like your evening meals should be nicer than a stale baked potato. ",
    "FTUE_WoM_WhoAreYou6": "Well, recently, some people got a bit too uppity about the whole affair. So rather than turn Draynor into rubble, I thought I might take myself on a nice little holiday to a continent no one's heard of. Should be fun I think. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_SurvivalHub1": "What can I help you with?",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_hub": "What do you want to know?",
    "PlayerChoice_Night": "What happens at night?",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_WhoAreYou4": "What matters is that we get you off to the best start you can. Warrior like yourself, can only be destined for glory. So let's make sure you know which end of the sword is the pointy bit, before you do yourself a mischief. You got any questions about the finer parts of battle, you come talk to me. I'll set you right. ",
    "PlayerChoice_WhatSecrets": "What secrets?",
    "FTUE_Zanik_BuildingAndCraftingLink": "What would you like to know?",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_NotGotGear2": "What you're wearing now, is not going to help you against the creatures you'll encounter.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Night1": "When the sun sets, Ashenfall's claws come out. More aggressive creatures roam the area and cold seeps in and saps your strength. ",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_NotBuiltBed5": "When you've done all that come back and see me. I'll give you something to help you on your journey.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_Intro_4": "When you've done that, craft yourself some air runes at the altar.",
    "PlayerChoice_Whoareyou": "Who are you?",
    "Zanik_FTUE_SeekingShelter_Postquest": "Why not expand your shelter and turn it into a proper home? You could add rooms, floors, really make something of it. ",
    "FTUE_Zanik_WhoAreYou1": "Yeah, right, hi! I'm Zanik. I'm a cave goblin explorer... well probably the cave goblin explorer... we don't get out much. ",
    "PlayerChoice_FirstSteps_AcceptTutorial": "Yes please [Begin Tutorial]",
    "FTUE_Zanik_Night2": "You can pass the night with a good sleep in bed. Wrap yourself up warm and dream away the danger until morning. ",
    "Doric_Prequest_generic": "You just walked right past the Wise Old Man there. Best go back and say hi, eh?",
    "Zanik_SeekingShelter_Intro_NotBuiltBed1": "You must be the newbie. I'm Zanik, it's a pleasure to meet you.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_MadeRunes_2": "You'll discover several spells as you improve your skills. Try experimenting with all of them. Magic is fun!",
    "FTUE_Vannaka_Block2": "You'll find blocking with a shield is the best defence. If you haven't got a shield, a weapon will do. ",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_AcceptTutorial_2": "You'll find them outside the temple. Check your map if you get lost, but he should be easy to spot.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_BuildThings2": "You'll need to create the pieces you'll want to place, then find where you want them to go and make sure they connect with one another.",
    "FTUE_Zanik_BuildThings1": "You'll need to gather materials first. Ash logs will do for a start, but better materials make for sturdier structures.",
    "Vannaka_Ratcatcher_Intro_NotGotFangs4": "You'll need to get yourself a decent weapon and perhaps a shield to take them down.",
    "Doric_RightTool_Intro_3": "You'll want to build yourself a workbench. Then once you've done that craft yourself a logging axe.",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_AcceptTutorial_1": "You'll want to get to grips with gathering and crafting first, Doric can help you with that.",
    "WoM_FirstSteps_Intro_2": "You've come at a great time. Heroic opportunities await. This long-forgotten place is just screaming to be explored.",
    "WoM_RuneMysteries_MadeRunes_1": "You've crafted some runes I see, good. Magic is a tool, just like any other, but one worth keeping around.",
    "Vannaka_ButterKnife_Intro_Default1": "You've dealt with some rats – well done – but they're small fry compared to everything else that's out there.",
    "SeekingShelter_Description": "Zanik wants to teach you some survival basics."
  },
  "QF_Vannaka_Dialogue": {
    "DogDays_Started_GotTokenAndRitualNotPurifiedToken_3": "A ritual of purification, to turn this sullied trinket into a true piece of the Antumnos, the ancestral home.",
    "DogDays_Started_HasPurifiedToken_1": "Ah, there it is. May I see it? The purified token?",
    "DogDays_Completed_DoesNotKnowWerewolf": "Ah, yes, sorry, this won't mean anything to you. Pay an old fool no mind.",
    "DogDays_NotKnowWerewolf_2": "Ah, yes, sorry, this won't mean anything to you. Pay an old fool no mind.",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_1": "Aye, yes. an explanation. See, the garou weren't always on Ashenfall. They came from far, far away.",
    "Objective5": "Bring the Purified King's Token to Vannaka in the Ghornfell Highlands.",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundToken_3": "But this... is almost what I'm looking for. A piece of Antumnos, though it seems... sullied, somehow.",
    "Objective2": "Challenge a Garou king in their Highland stronghold and claim their token.",
    "Objective4": "Complete the ritual of purification on the King's Token at the ancient shrine where \"a heart once beat\".",
    "DogDays_Intro_KingsTokenUnpurified_4": "Could you look into this? Check the garou camps, beneath the spines of great wyrm remains. Let me know if you uncover anything.",
    "QuestTitle": "Dog Days",
    "PlayerChoice_DontPerformTheRitual": "Don't perform the Ritual of Purification",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands_4": "Even I would think twice about trying to hunt one of those down. But here, the garou make their bones their home.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands_1": "Few places embody \"survival of the fittest\" quite like here.",
    "DogDays_RitualPerformed": "For a fraction of a moment the shrine is bathed in ethereal moonlight that shines from the ritual writing engraved on its surface. The King's Token seems different somehow, cleaner, lighter and somehow whole.",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundRitual_1": "Found anything interesting yet, young pup? Hrmm, some writing on a ritual? Let me take a look...",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundToken_1": "Found anything interesting yet, young pup? Hrmm, you took a token from a garou king?",
    "DogDays_Starteed_NoProgress_1": "Found anything interesting yet, young pup? No? Pity. Perhaps take a look through some of the garou camps?",
    "DogDays_Started_GotTokenAndRitualNotPurifiedToken_1": "Found anything interesting yet, young pup? Oh? You have the king's token? Let me see...",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_6": "Here, something to show my gratitude for this piece of family history.",
    "DogDays_FullInventory": "Hrmm, looks like you're carrying too much, young pup. Best lighten your load before I can give you this. ",
    "DogDays_WhatIsAntumnos_4": "I believe the garou lived there once, before their goddess took them here.",
    "DogDays_Intro_KingsTokenUnpurified_3": "I came here to uncover the truth. I heard tale of a ritual to preserve a fragment of a legacy my family has forgotten.",
    "DogDays_Intro_NoProgress_1": "I came here to uncover the truth. I heard tale of a ritual to preserve a fragment of a legacy my family has forgotten.",
    "PlayerChoice_IDontNeedAnExplanation": "I don't need an explanation.",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_5": "I don't want to hide any more. And this trinket will be a link to my ancestors, something to help me make peace with the beast.",
    "DogDays_Completed_KnowsWerewolf_2": "I have run from my wolf my entire life. Feared its fangs and claws. But, now, perhaps I can allow myself to face it.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheGarou_2": "I know, I know. What does a slayer master care about spirituality? But that's exactly the point, you see...",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_4": "I left my people to try and hide from the beast, but it's always followed me... and been used against me.",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundToken_4": "I need you to look around, see if there's anything you can do to purify it. To make it a pure piece of that long lost place.",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundRitual_4": "I'll explain everything once you do. .",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundToken_2": "I'm impressed, that's no easy feat, that. Defeating a garou king.",
    "DogDays_Intro_NoProgress_2": "I've been scouring garou camps, but I need your help and, well, a burden shared is a burden halved, eh?",
    "DogDays_Started_GotTokenAndRitualNotPurifiedToken_4": "I... I need you to do this for me, young pup. Complete that ritual and purify the token. I'll explain everything on your return.",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundRitual_3": "I... this is important to me, young pup. I ask that you keep looking. See if you can complete this ritual and bring me the token.",
    "QuestDescription": "Investigate the Garou and their rituals.",
    "DogDays_WhatIsAntumnos_3": "It has always been of interest to me, ever since my mother told me legends of such a place when I was a child.",
    "DogDays_Completed_1": "It is strange how a simple trinket can give you such a strong sense of connection. It feels like a piece of me pining for home.",
    "DogDays_WhyIntestedInRituals_1": "It's a personal matter. An old family interest, shall we say?",
    "DogDays_Started_GotTokenAndRitualNotPurifiedToken_2": "It's not quite right. It feels tainted, as if it's forgotten where it's from. Wait... that ritual you found, that's the answer!",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheGarou_3": "Like we slayer masters, the garou are primal creatures. We understand the need to be hunter, not prey.",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_3": "My ancesters... the werewolves. Aye, yes, my biggest secret. Tooth and claw beneath the silvery moon.",
    "DogDays_WhyIntestedInRituals_2": "My family has a history with the beastmen, dating back over the ages.",
    "DogDays_Completed_NotInterested_1": "No, you're right, I'm sorry to trouble you. Here, something to thank you for your effort.",
    "DogDays_WhatIsAntumnos_2": "One in which the wild grows free and unhindered by the yoke of so called \"civilisation\".",
    "DogDays_RitualText": "Our Kings, who have ruled at the highest peak for generations, each carry a single piece of home with them. From the old home where our ancestors came from, there is a single pebble in the token that the king wears about their neck. Over time and exposure to this land, that pebble becomes corrupted and tainted by this place. \r\n\r\nBut corruption can be purged. Rot can be cut away. \r\n\r\nSeek the altar that sits where a heart once beat. Pillars of bone reaching for the sky, longing to touch the moon in memory of the lost one. There, her power echoes still, able to wash away the stain of this world. \r\n\r\nPlace ram horns, two of them, as an image of the goddess so that her power has a vessel to work the miracle. Anoint then the token with the oil of the lapis vine, crushing three of the bulbs over the token. Storm and oil, anathema to the corruption. \r\n\r\nOffer a prayer in memory of her. Lougrim, the Huntress in moonlight, is gone but not forgotten. Do this and a piece of home shall be once again restored.\r\n\r\nSuch is the way of our kings who rule on high, closest to the sky and the memory of her silvered radiance. \r\n",
    "PlayerChoice_PerformRitual": "Perform the Ritual of Purification",
    "RitualTitle": "Ritual Of Purification",
    "DogDays_RitualTitle": "Ritual of Purification",
    "Objective1": "Search Garou camps beneath giant wyrm bones in the Highlands for information on Garou ritual practices.",
    "Objective3": "Search garou camps beneath the giant wyrm bones in the Highlands for information on the King's Token.",
    "Objective6": "Search the Ghornfell Highlands for a friendly face with an interest in Garou rituals.",
    "DogDays_Completed_Explanation_2": "Sometime in the third age, I think, they were captured by Zamorakian forces and there they became part of a vampyre experiment, to create something new.",
    "DogDays_Completed_KnowsWerewolf_1": "The animal within me, remembering a part of itself. And, for the first time in as long as I can remember, the beast does not stir.",
    "DogDays_NotKnowWerewolf_1": "The animal within me, remembering a part of itself. And, for the first time in as long as I can remember, the beast does not stir.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheGarou_4": "The garou honour that truth, in every part of their culture. I find it... comforting.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands_2": "The garou, the wildlife, even the very weather wants you dead. This place makes you face your mortality, lets you know you're alive.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands_3": "The whole place is littered with the bones of great wyrms. Beasts so terrible I'm glad they're dead.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands_5": "There's something beautiful about that, in a weird sort of way. Sheltering the shadow of monsters slain.",
    "DogDays_Starteed_NoProgress_2": "They make their homes in the spines of the dead wyrms around here, why not give them a look?.",
    "DogDays_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheGarou_1": "They may seem brutal and savage, the garou, and frankly they are -- But there's a deeper spirituality to them as well.",
    "DogDays_Intro_NoProgress_3": "They tend to camp beneath the spines of great wyrm remains. Scout those bones and let me know if you uncover anything.",
    "DogDays_Intro_KingsTokenUnpurified_2": "This is a piece of the ancestral world of the garou, but it's been corrupted by this world and needs purification.",
    "DogDays_LougrimShrine_NotFoundRitual": "This shrine appears to be part of a garou ritual of some kind. ",
    "DogDays_LougrimShrine_NotGotIngredients": "This shrine is dedicated to Lougrim, and looks like the place referred to in the Ritual of Purification. If you had the King's Token, 2 ram horns and 3 shock bulbs, you could perform the ritual here. ",
    "DogDays_LougrimShrine_GotRitualGotToken_GotIngredients": "This shrine is dedicated to Lougrim, and looks like the place referred to in the Ritual of Purification. You have everything you need to perform the ritual. ",
    "DogDays_Started_FoundRitual_2": "This... this is what I'm looking for. A ritual to take a piece of Antumnos, the primordial forest.",
    "DogDays_Intro_FoundOnlyRitual_2": "This... this is what I've been looking for. A chance to own a piece of the Ancestral world.",
    "DogDays_Started_HasPurifiedToken_2": "This... this trinket may seem like nothing to you. But for me it's an anchor to my ancestral home...",
    "DogDays_Intro_KingsTokenPurified_1": "Wait... that token. May I see it? The purified token?",
    "DogDays_Intro_KingsTokenUnpurified_1": "Wait... that token. You've slain their king? May I see the token? Yes, yes, I thought so. This is almost what I'm looking for. Almost.",
    "PlayerChoice_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheGarou": "What can you tell me about the Garou?",
    "PlayerChoice_WhatCanYouTellMeAboutTheHighlands": "What can you tell me about the Highlands?",
    "PlayerChoice_WhatDoYouMean": "What do you mean?",
    "PlayerChoice_WhatIsAntumnos": "What's Antumnos?",
    "DogDays_Intro_FoundOnlyRitual_1": "What? You've uncovered a ritual text? Let me take a look at that.",
    "DogDays_WhatIsAntumnos_1": "Where, might be better. It is the primordial forest, a world far far from ours.",
    "PlayerChoice_WhyInterestedInRituals": "Why are you interested in garou rituals?",
    "DogDays_Intro_Default_1": "You've come a long way, young pup, good to see. I'm here studying a race not seen for hundreds of years - the Garou.",
    "DogDays_Intro_FoundOnlyRitual_3": "Young pup, please, you must complete this ritual for me. I... I cannot say why, just yet, but it is important to me.",
    "DogDays_Intro_FoundOnlyRitual_4": "Your journey begins with the death of the garou king. Go! Paint the earth with his blood. History favours the bold, and the bold carve their legend into the bones of the fallen."
  },
  "QF_Zanik_Dialogue": {
    "QFWormelbowGiveFood1": "Ah, that hit the spot. Been proper starvin ever since I got meself locked up.",
    "QFWormelbowGiveFood5": "Bet you'd find out if you took a pickaxe to their rock-like heads, haha. Go on, steal this lots poxy treasure. They got it comin' they does.",
    "QFWormelbowRefuseFood": "Bleh, I thought so. Get lost then. I got better things to do. ",
    "Objective_talktozanik": "Bring what you've discovered to Zanik. ",
    "QFBilegutQuestCompleted": "Don't distract me, I's workin on me poetry. Hrmm, what rhymes with offal?",
    "QFBilegutIntroNotGotItem2": "Eer, you wanna get your 'ands on sommit shiny? I'll tells ya where you cans find it. Ya just gorra do me a little favour first. ",
    "QFBiletgutTaskStartedGotItem2": "Ere, let me tells ya where they hide their treasure. It'll be hidden behind a damaged wall, probably badly repaired. ",
    "QFWormelbowGiveFoodAnswer": "Great, I'm starving!",
    "QFBilegutIntroGotItem2": "Haha! Good goin' human, steal their sacred thing. This lot don't deserve no divine thingamy. ",
    "QFWormelbowGiveFood4": "Heh, you should steal it. It'll be a right laugh if you do. They keep their secrets well buried this lot, don't want anyone knowing their business. ",
    "QFWormelbowGiveFood2": "I were searchin' for a treasure, ya see. A secret bauble this lot keep hidden. Thought it might give my tribe the edge.",
    "Objective_investigatestrongholds": "Investigate the goblin strongholds at Brynmoor Castle and the Adventurer's guild",
    "QFBilegutSpokeToNoItems": "Killed enough of these plonkers yet? Nah? Bring me five of them packs they carry, then we'll talk. ",
    "QFBilegutIntroGotItem1": "Oh lookie here, a human. Wait... what's that you got there? Ain't that their special shiny treasure?",
    "QFBilegutIntroNotGotItem1": "Oh, lookie here, a human. Don't get many o'you lot round these parts. Not unless you is parts o'course, haha.",
    "QFWormelbowGiveFood3": "Oh. Haha. I just had meself a funny idea. ",
    "QFReliquaryFail": "There's nothing of interest here. ",
    "QFBilegutIntroNotGotItem4": "They carry these packs around wi'em. Kill em and bring me five of those and then I'll share me secrets. Fair?",
    "QFBilegutTastStartedGotItem3": "They'll have stashed it behind it. Not the best hiding place, my lot are much smarter. ",
    "QFBilegutIntroNotGotItem3": "This lot, rival tribe you see, 'ave been awfully rude to me. If you gut em all, like the fish they is, then I'll tells ya where the shiny thing is.",
    "QFReliquaryGive": "You find a strange amulet with the symbol of Bandos on it.",
    "QFBiletgutTaskCompleted": "You gottem all! Killed every last one of the smarmy gits. I likes you. ",
    "QFBiletgutTaskStartedGotItem1": "You gottem all! Killed every last one of the smarmy gits. I likes you. "
  },
