  "ST_Fellhollow_LoreScraps": {
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.5.Text": "Avisk is a snake! I am not surprised by this discovery, he’s never been subtle about his ambition, but that he would dare to attempt an experiment on Viika, well that’s unforgivable.\r\n\r\nHe attached tubes, crystals and all sorts of nonsense to my sibling’s head and attempted something with rune essence that caused a lot of explosions. Viika was hurt, burned across their temple and one of their wings is damaged enough that they might never fly again.\r\n\r\nI have never felt anger like I did in that moment. Even the rage from the curse never struck me as hard. In that instant I dragged blades of ice from the aether, and I would have torn Avisk to pieces of only my sibling hadn’t said “no”. Always too gentle Viika, not like the rest of us.\r\n\r\nMaybe that’s why they never partook Rasthin’s discovery. Because they knew what monsters we’d become.\r\n\r\nAvisk won’t get away without consequences. My sibling may be gentle, but I am not. I flow like the river and wield the patience of glaciers, and Avisk will learn that water always wins.",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.3.Text": "Avisk is like the scales behind my wings, irritating and in desperate needs of a good scratch. He keeps coming to me and trying to explain to me how I need to do X with the dragons, or Y with their eggs, as if he, an Aughra, has the slightest understanding of real science. Imbecile.\r\n\r\nHis obsession with crystals is growing increasingly tiresome. \r\n\r\nHe’s already messed with some of the brood, tried to use that strange rune essence in ways that would cause energy to flow in certain ways. I can see the concept he’s going for, but his clumsy nonsense just leads it to ruin. Trying to create some sort of enhanced mind for the dragons, as if they could exist like a swarm. \r\n\r\nAll of them, of course, died. All but one, and she’s turned out strangely.\r\n\r\nI encourage the growth of a single head for the dragons, keeps them sane and stable. There’s no good that can come from multiple brains in charge of one body, yet she proves me wrong. All the minds work as if connected, as if part of the same whole. A single consciousness spread across all of them. A single personality.\r\n\r\nBecause that’s what it is, a personality. A will. A mind of her own. She is enraged, yes, like all dragons are, but she spreads it across herself, weakening the effect. I have encountered curiosity, reason, even wit. A most curious creature, I look forward to studying her more.",
    "Fellhollow.VaultPuzzle.1.Text": "Avisk keeps trying to sneak into my laboratory, convinced that the secrets within will grant him the knowledge to transcend his mortal frame. I’ve told him time and time again that it will do no such thing, but he’s convinced I conceal my discoveries, hoarding knowledge and sharing it with none.\r\n\r\nHave my advances not brought this little group to the heights of success? It was my work that allowed Rasthin to complete her device. My work that created armies of dragons to serve at our beck and call. Yet, despite all this, he’s convinced that I keep the really good stuff to myself.\r\n\r\nThe irritating part is, of course, that he is correct.\r\n\r\nSo, I seal it away behind locked doors shielded from even dragonkin magic. A mechanism that will stand for eternity, barring him access.\r\n\r\nThe best part is that I based the lock not on a key, which he could steal, nor on a phrase, which he could overhear, but upon a riddle posed to me by the priest Kranon, all those years ago.\r\n\r\n“What does the charitable priest offer, the illuminated sage seek, and the ignorant forsake? Walk their paths and what do you discover?”\r\n\r\nHe will go mad knowing the answer, for it is obvious, yet it is the steps one must walk to get there that will unbar his path. I bet he’ll even think the damaged statue is accidental wear and tear.\r\n\r\nIt will drive him mad. Just thinking about his frustration makes me giddy with delight.  ",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.4.Title": "Battered Diary",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.3.Title": "Captain Rainer's Journal",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.2.Text": "Death leaves its mark on the world. You feel it around graveyards, mausoleums and on the remnants of ancient battlefields that claimed hundreds of lives. It’s a pressure that presses against the air and weighs you down. Here the air is crushing, I feel myself being dragged to the floor by the grief and the rage attached to these bones.\r\n\r\nXikotal, Imaru’s mate, lies here dead and gone. His soul long since passed to the Afterlife, leaving Imaru alone and angry. Perhaps he was lucky to pass before seeing his mate like this. See the monster she has become since her death.\r\n\r\nStill, this grief makes a powerful fetter. A thread of connection strong enough to forge a seal. I’ll lay it here, in this vault, protected from the dead by the dragonkin guardians. Hopefully that will keep it safe enough that no one can set this dread dragon free.",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.2.Text": "Dragon-Hybridisation Experiment Day 7\r\n\r\nIt is not easy splicing reptile and mammal together, their very nature fights against their biology and they would rather perish upon emergence than live with such a hybrid nature. It’s a shame really, the little pups are quite cute. I think Viika would like one as a pet, it might keep my sibling grounded and anchored a little more to our frame of reference. Wishful thinking perhaps.\r\n\r\nThe wolves have proved remarkably durable, considering. While they all die seconds after birth, they do hold on longer than expected. I attempted to combine kebbit and dragon and… well… that didn’t go well. Chinchompa and dragon, that was a mistake that will take some time to repair – I liked that lab.  Yet wolf, there’s something here, I can feel it. They’re resilient, dangerous and there’s something in the pack mentality that fascinates me.\r\n\r\nDragon-Hybridisation Experiment Day 56\r\n\r\nI have decided that a rapid hybridisation approach will not work. Mammals, while fast breeders, are weak and lack the resilience needed to survive the experiment if I go too quickly. Instead I shall engineer a slow breeding process, spreading the development out over the generations.\r\n\r\nTedious, yes, but at least it will allow me to focus on other project while this progresses.\r\n\r\nDragon-Hybridisation Experiment Day 219\r\n\r\nThe changes are gradual, yet viable. Scales here and there, some improved musculature and reflexes, yet nothing approaching the power of a dragon.\r\n\r\nIs this all they can be?\r\n\r\nDragon-Hybridisation Experiment Day 2307\r\n\r\nI’d forgotten about this failure of an experiment. The dragon-wolves have proved inadequate for any useful purpose. I was going to incinerate the remaining members, but Viika in a fit of strangeness released them all.\r\n\r\nSo, now we have it. Dragon-wolves running all over the region, lovely. Honestly my sibling can be so vexing sometimes.",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.3.Title": "Dragon-embossed Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.2.Text": "Dragons are a useful tool, but little more than that. They are powerful, yes, strong and dangerous, excellent beasts of burden or disposable troops in a fight. Yet, they lack the grace, poise and power needed to be new dragonkin hosts. I always knew that was a failed plan.\r\n\r\nStill, what experiment cannot be perfected? What hypothesis cannot be refined? There is something in dragons, some key to our apotheosis, that I feel driven to explore further still.\r\n\r\nAnd Rasthin has the blood that may be the key.\r\n\r\n“Gods”, they call them, what a nonsense affair. Leave that to the waning priest caste, like that mewling fool Kranon, and the primitive spirits these lesser beings follow. They are powerful creatures, formed of a changed and ascended essence, as if flesh and soul merged into a single construct and solidified into form.\r\n\r\nOne of them bleeds. Perhaps all of them, but this one for certain. She calls herself a goddess of the moon and the primordial hunt. Nonsense, of course, moons are rocks floating in the emptiness and there’s nothing spiritual or metaphysical about a predator seeking lunch.\r\n\r\nStill, if I can refine this power? If I can merge it with a dragon, perhaps… just perhaps… I can turn these worthless dragons into something we can use.",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.2.Text": "Duneday\r\n\r\nUlgo made friends with man in the woods. Could not see face but they were very friendly. Made lots of pretty noises at Ulgo, though Ulgo does not know their words.\r\n\r\nTomorrow Ulgo is going to go and see if they want to play catch with him. Papa says that everyone loves playing catch, even though the villagers need to stand very far away so that the ball does not hurt them.\r\n\r\nThrew stone once, because had no ball, and villager wouldn’t talk to me again after. Ulgo very sad. Villager never spoken to Ulgo again, so Ulgo cannot even say sorry.\r\n\r\nTwiblick\r\n\r\nUlgo’s friend was in the woods again. Got a better look at him, his skin was all shiny and special. Maybe he got paints? Ulgo will ask Papa if he can get paints.\r\n\r\nFriend in wood played very rough. When Ulgo threw him the ball, he did not throw it back. Instead he ran at Ulgo and tried to wrestle. Ulgo only ten, but Ulgo very strong, Papa always says so, and Ulgo push friend away.\r\n\r\nFun game. Laughed a lot. Even though new friend bit me a few times. Must have gotten overexcited. Ulgo understand, Ulgo bite too.\r\n\r\nIvanday\r\n\r\nUlgo hungry. Feel slow and strange. Need to eat more. Maybe Mama make Ulgo something.\r\n\r\nDuneday\r\n\r\nUlgo hungry. Papa’s arm taste bad.\r\n\r\nNotduneday\r\n\r\nUlgo hungry.\r\n\r\nDay\r\n\r\nUlgo hungry.",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.2.Title": "Experiment Log",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.1.Title": "Farmer Fred's Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.6.Text": "Fellhollow is doomed, there’s no other word for it. Imaru’s wedged herself in this part of the underworld and her mouth is wide and consuming all the souls that flow down the river Noumenon. With each soul she devours she grows stronger and her grip tightens. Her hunger grows, she craves more and more, and she’ll never stop.\r\n\r\nThe necromantic energies of the Underworld then wash back through the Blessing and into her subjects, animating their bodies and filling them with an unquenchable thirst for more souls. They’re nothing but withered husks of themselves, all humanity drained away and all that’s left is a terrible, clawing, need.\r\n\r\nI’ve seen this before, in the forbidden texts that my master kept hidden from me. Only the source of this evil isn’t some nebulous power that dwells in the shadows, but an undead dragon. An evil of my own making.\r\n\r\nSo, one I must undo. I cannot break the curse. I cannot end her wrath. For all my skills I am nowhere near a match for her in battle.  All I can do is protect the rest of Ashenfall, and Gielinor, by keeping her locked away.\r\n\r\nIt’ll take some work, but the one thing I have in abundance is time.",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.4.Text": "He’s dead, the black-scaled guardian. As he died it was as if the wind stilled in mourning, a great silence spread across the land dragging away all motion and noise. Leaves stopped, as if frozen in the moment. Clouds halted staring down at it all in horror. Everything was silent… except for her sorrow.\r\n\r\nThe lament of a dragon is primal, perhaps even primordial. Our lizard-brains bow their heads in mournful empathy for her suffering. It is as if a wave of misery crashes against all of us, drenching us to our bones in grief.\r\n\r\nThe writhing heads of Queen Kuldra, the Godeater, laughs from the sky. Her echoing mockery felt by every living creature in Fellhollow, as if we’re all a joke to her. A passing diversion, before she destroys us all.\r\n\r\nShe doesn’t, because that would be kind. She does not end Imaru’s pain, not yet. She leaves her with the agony of loss and the dissolution of her dreams for the future. A cruel punishment, for the simple crime of peace. She dared to shelter the lost and wandering humans, rather than put us to the flame.\r\n\r\nEmpathy, her only sin, and for that she must endure a loss so deep we may never understand it. How do you survive eternities together, ripped away in an instant?",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.4.Text": "I am guilty of mistakes, I admit this. I let things get to me and I don’t think them through as well as I should. When I lost Ulv I tried to bring him back and… well… the result of that is better buried, I confess.\r\n\r\nI visit him from time to time. There’s nothing left of my friend there, hasn’t been for some time, but I don’t want him getting lonely.\r\n\r\nShe was my next mistake. Imaru. After the death of her mate she came to me seeking a way to bring him back. Necromancy doesn’t work like that, at least not yet and certainly not within my skill set. Yet, still, I thought I could offer her something almost as good.\r\n\r\nI offered her revenge.\r\n\r\nI created a curse within her, using her grief and rage as a focus, so that it might strengthen her against Kuldra. She was to become a devouring force that would feast on the Godeater’s very soul.\r\n\r\nIt did not work.\r\n\r\nKuldra is stronger than I imagined. Her essence more powerful than either of us could have guessed. As Imaru raged at her Kuldra simply laughed and rebuffed her, barely even registering the unholy force hurled against her. She is a monster, and I use that word very rarely.\r\n\r\nSo Imaru died. Fell to the ground in a crumbled heap… and I wish that were the end of it.",
    "Fellhollow.VaultPuzzle.2.Text": "I am lost in these treacherous ruins, with all hope of the outside world lost to me. I sought to escape the horror of Fellhollow, but this place is worse. Rotting from within. \r\n\r\nYet, as I wither… as these bonds of flesh are broken, another world reveals itself. \r\n\r\nWalkways, doorways, entire new paths to travel. This prison is filled with ways to run that were not there before. \r\n\r\nStill, as I explore them, I feel her gaze upon me. I feel her hunger grow. Imaru is watching, and there is no escape. \r\n\r\nSaradomin have mercy, because Imaru most certainly will not. ",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.6.Text": "I am still here. I am still here.\r\n\r\nI am still me. I am still me.\r\n\r\nI am withering and I cannot hold it back.\r\n\r\nIt begins with silence behind the eyes, as if there’s nothing there but the most basic of needs – the need to feed. More and more of us, ever since Imaru’s defeat and death at Kuldra’s claws, feels part of ourselves slipping away. I am dragged outside my being, I am drawn beyond my skull, my skin, myself.\r\n\r\nAnd the world changes the more I am pulled away.\r\n\r\nI see things that were not there before. Flickers, out of the corner of my eye. Doors that were not doors before. I see a great river undulating and flowing but rising and flooding as though something is blocked within it and forcing it to overflow.\r\n\r\nBut the worst is that feeling, of eyes upon me. As if something is not just watching me but focused on me. A predator waiting to strike.\r\n\r\nI’ve seen what happens to those consumed by it. They walk still, but there is no life there, only hunger. A need to grab, claw and rend the living, desperate for a piece of the soul that seems lost.\r\n\r\nIn my bones I feel a tug, a current, drawing the part of me that’s… me… away.\r\n\r\nI don’t want to become one of those monsters.\r\n\r\nI am still here. I am still here.\r\n\r\nI am still me. I am still me.",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.1.Text": "I fled, like the coward I am, back toward Bramblemead, back to the hatred. Yet, the way is closed. A great wall bars my path. I am a prisoner here among the damned.\r\n\r\nWe all tried so hard to stem the tide. The Wild Knights to the east pushed back against the horde as much as they could. They walled themselves away in their keep  until no one remains alive to guard it.\r\n\r\nEmberwood sealed itself away behind a barrier, priests working together in unified cause. Faith locks everyone out, and everyone in.\r\n\r\nAs for the tower, and those who dwelled beside it, it’s shattered. The dragons’ disciples lost in a great lake of sorrow and grief. Damned by their own devotion.\r\n\r\nAnd here I am, clawing at a wall, mere metres of stone between safety and despair. Despair always wins.\r\n\r\nPerhaps it is like those doors? I see them sometimes, out of the corner of my eye. Strange and ephemeral, inviting me in. Yet, if I focus on them, I see nothing. Only when I feel myself slipping away do they show themselves again. Perhaps a wall is not always a wall, like a door is not always there?\r\n\r\nIt doesn’t matter. I am lost. Fellhollow is lost.\r\n\r\nIt’s all her fault.",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.3.Text": "I found an egg today, buried in the earth. Looks like it fell out of one of them there ruins, you know, the ones under the ground with the glowy blue flames? Well there was this egg that was just sticking out of this weird little pot and so I took it, you know? Thought it might make a good omelette or something. Scarius says that I’m being stupid, but he just wants to omelette for himself.\r\n\r\n…\r\n\r\nOK, so, right, omelette is a no go. Tried to crack the egg, no dice. Smashed it with a hammer. Still nothing. Sword? No chance. So I figured it might make a nice ornament or something, keep the barracks nice and decorative like.\r\n\r\n…\r\n\r\nEgg hatched today. Coincidentally, on the same day I lost two of my fingers. I get it though, poor thing was hungry, can’t begrudge a baby the occasional nip. Little green thing, scales and all, reckon it’s a dragon. Seems like a nice one though.\r\n\r\nCaptain wants me to kill it, but I’m not gonna do that. Poor thing just needs some love and some steak from the kitchen and they’ll be a good little beastie.\r\n\r\nNeed a name for them. Maybe Fang because they’ve got enough of them.\r\n\r\n…\r\n\r\nCaptain acting strange today. Came back from the town all shaking and weird, says there’s some sort of infection or other, people going weird. I’m sure it’s nothing to worry about, I’ll just focus on keeping Fang well hidden. Don’t want anyone to know what I’ve done.",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.1.Text": "I had always wanted neighbours, out here in the sticks, but these weren’t exactly what I imagined. Refugees, so they claim, from the Bandosian forces, escaped the violence of their people in hope of peace.\r\n\r\nFollowers of the war god, looking to settle down. I didn’t believe it, until they turned in their weapons. There was this great pile of them outside the village, built up into a pyre and then set to the flame.\r\n\r\nWe danced as they burned, it was beautiful. I drank with a few of them and… well… I don’t remember much of the evening anymore. Just hazy moments of laughter and stories, nothing more than that.\r\n\r\nNow I bring Golbor and Klom baskets of pumpkins and in exchange they help me plough the fields before we can sow the soil anew. Good people. Full of laughter and big emotions so large they create a gravity that draws all of us in.\r\n\r\nThese weren’t the neighbours I imagined, but I couldn’t ask for better.",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.3.Text": "I have a new customer, and she won’t fit through the door.\r\n\r\nOdd to empathise with a dragon, but I do. We all saw what happened. I watched as the great multi-headed dragon queen pulled Xikotal’s heart from his chest and ate it in front of his mate.\r\n\r\nYou don’t just get over something like that. It’s visceral and cuts you deeper than you ever thought possible. It’s not just grief. It’s not just rage. The two forces combine into something new, something stronger than the sum of its components. That sort of feeling is powerful – strong enough to change you into something other than what you were.\r\n\r\nI have lived for longer than I can say on that feeling alone. It’s a fuel that rages within you, burning you from the inside to keep you warm. I can only imagine what it’s doing to a creature like her.\r\n\r\nShe asks me to bring her beloved back, but that’s beyond my power, always has been. I’ve never been great at animating the dead, I can do a few bones, sure, but nothing stronger.\r\n\r\nCurses, though, that I’m good with those.\r\n\r\nImaru’s rage makes her the perfect focus. The beating heart around the darkest magics. She can be a weapon against the Godeater, if I hone her right. The rage of a dragon, combined with the power of a grief-curse, such a thing could be the blade needed to slit Kuldra’s throat.\r\n\r\nI will forge her carefully.",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.5.Text": "I have heard about the God Wars, in the stories that Grandfather gives. He passed them down from his father and his father before that, tales of epic battles and destructive forces beyond reason. This must have been what clashes between gods felt like.\r\n\r\nImaru and Kuldra, raging against one another using Ashenfall as a weapon. The wind became knives, the rocks hurled as cannon-fire, and the rain turned to hail, falling like great-hammers on everyone caught in their path. Cataclysmic powers crash against one another and each blow feels like it might tear the continent apart.\r\n\r\nShe feels different this time, Imaru. Changed. Like her grief and her rage have been forged into weapons and she slams them against the Godeater with unbridled hate. In response, Kuldra laughs, even though her armour shudders against the force of it, scales falling to the earth like the beginning flakes of winter snow.\r\n\r\nThere is a sensation in my chest -- strength being leeched from within me as Imaru presses the attack. I see old Mrs. Mossfoot stumble, hand across her chest, as each of the other villagers feel it too. The Blessing, a source of strength, now feels like a hole in each of us, draining us dry.\r\n\r\nBut for Imaru we’ll endure it. Against Kuldra we’ll stand.\r\n\r\nFellhollow does not fall this day!",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.3.Text": "I have seen what love looks like, and it spirals through the clouds. Serpentine patterns entwined together as they dance in the sun’s rays and share the sky with one another. For such large creatures, you would think them incapable of grace, yet I have never seen a dance so beautiful as the two of them together.\r\n\r\nMy grandmother speaks of their dance with a smile on her wrinkled lips. Telling stories of how the villagers danced the same, hand in hand, around the dark fires of winter. Bringing love and hope and joy in a musical war against the dark. Yet, there is a knowing sort of sadness when I ask where the dragons' children are.\r\n\r\nBecause I have never seen them.\r\n\r\nPerhaps that’s why they are so kind to us. So gentle. Why they crush the bandits as they ransack our villages, or why they toss the dragon wolves out into the cold. Because we are their children, in a strange sort of way.\r\n\r\nGran says that’s what the Blessing is, that little dragon magic in our bones. An enchantment woven over each of us, as part of the dance. It makes us healthier, makes us heartier, makes us better than before.\r\n\r\nI can’t wait to learn a dance of my own. Perhaps I can spiral through the clouds like they do, wouldn’t that be a wonderful thing?",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.1.Text": "I wonder, sometimes, whether we are too limited in our focus. Is the cold-blooded nature of the reptile, more useful than the mammalian warm-blood approach? I watch the creatures of this region, the kebbits, the cows, the sheep and I see how they multiply and spread at a pace that far exceeds our own.\r\n\r\nBy contrast, the dragons I birth are a slow and laborious effort. Each one must be carefully managed and maintained with focused precision. Even those capable of spawning their own young, do so slowly. Often brooding no more than a single viable progeny in a century of practice.\r\n\r\nEven my prize specimen produced only a single heir, a red-scaled whelp, no less, unlike his mother’s multicoloured hues. Perhaps the fault lies in the father. I should dissect him and see where the problem begins.\r\n\r\nBut I lose my train of thought. Mammals. Noisy, smelly, but they are everywhere, breeding like rats – which are also mammals, now I think about it. Perhaps I should turn my sights on them instead.\r\n\r\nThere are a pack of dire wolves that wander near my laboratory, it would be simple enough to procure a few of their number. Some adults, a few children, I’ll need a large and diverse sample size for my experiments.\r\n\r\nPerhaps there’s a place where reptile and mammal can meet, to create a superior creature. I shall investigate further.",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.1.Text": "It is a strange thing to leave one’s home. All those old comforts, those familiar sights, smells and memories, just left behind. Stranger still, is leaving because you just don’t recognise it anymore.\r\n\r\nWere we always so cruel? So callous and so shortsighted that we turn on our own just because they’re a little bit strange? So Jenna has seaweed for hair and eyes of literal sapphire. Isn’t that something to love about her, rather than hate?\r\n\r\nHome is changed now. Those familiar sights are stained in horrid crimson. Those sentimental scents are tainted with a worrying touch of iron. Memories incinerated by rising flames, burning hope just as old neighbours burn away the homes of everyone different.\r\n\r\nSo we leave. We go north. Past the garou who snarl even though we have a treaty, and then down into the deep dark of the earth in search of a new home. One we pray will stand longer than the last.\r\n\r\nA home we can be proud of.",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.1.Title": "Laboratory Note",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.5.Title": "Lacrussa's Diary",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.1.Title": "Lacrussa's Journal",
    "Fellhollow.VaultPuzzle.1.Title": "Lacrussa's Memoir",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.2.Title": "Lacrussa's Notes",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.3.Title": "Lacrussa's Ravings",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.4.Title": "Lacrussa's Writings",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.2.Title": "Lazilly-penned Diary",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.1.Title": "Mould-covered Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.3.Text": "Of all the horrors of the rising dead, none are quite so chilling as the enormous undead ogres that now roam the lands. While all the vile undead seem filled with a hunger they can never sate, these beasts have a hunger greater than any other, and a terrifying capacity to consume.\r\n\r\nSome of the scouts first saw them near the village borders, trying to break through the barricades to gain entry. Ogres are terrifying at the best of times, even the peaceful refugees who settled here, and these are scarier still.\r\n\r\nIt’s like gazing up at a wall made of muscle, that wants, more than anything, to eat you alive. There is no malice behind their eyes. No cruelty. There is just emptiness and hunger and the understanding that you might be lunch.\r\n\r\nWhat scares me most about these creatures, is that their undead nature defies the theories we’d been working under. Since it was the villagers who first began to change, we assumed that it must be something to do with the strange magic their dragon patron worked upon them. Since most of us had not undergone this so-called “Blessing”, we thought we were safe from this terrifying transformation.\r\n\r\nYet, these… zogres… throw that theory out the window. They received no blessing, so how can that be the source?\r\n\r\nAnd if they can be affected, then surely so can we?\r\n\r\nPerhaps that would explain why I’m getting hungrier, no matter how much I eat. If that’s the case… then we’re all doomed. Fellhollow will fall.",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.5.Title": "Priestly Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.5.Title": "Ravanna's Fifth Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.1.Title": "Ravanna's First Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.4.Title": "Ravanna's Fourth Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.2.Title": "Ravanna's Second Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.7.Title": "Ravanna's Seventh Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.6.Title": "Ravanna's Sixth Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.3.Title": "Ravanna's Third Journal",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.4.Title": "Red-stained Diary",
    "Fellhollow.VaultPuzzle.2.Title": "Rot-covered Journal",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.5.Text": "Scripture says that all gods other than Saradomin are false, and their cultists are not to be trusted. Yet, I don’t see it that way today. As the village has fallen to the shambling nightmare that is the withering, the other priests and I have worked together to save who we can.\r\n\r\nThere are dead buried deep below the soil and their bones carry the power of prayer in them, like all do. So we priests prayed together, a union of faith, to erect a barrier of belief to keep the withered villagers contained.\r\n\r\nOur prayers bound to the icons, and only together will the village be re-opened once more.\r\n\r\nA tragic loss, truly. Emberwood could have been the great human utopia. Faiths working side by side. Amalgamated and not – villagers who do not let their differences define them. Two great dragons, to watch over us and keep us safe. It could have been perfect.\r\n\r\nBut belief needs adversity, or it becomes complacency. This will be a trial for each of us that we must strive to overcome.",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.2.Text": "So this is what the people who left Bramblemead are up to. Honestly, it seems like a pretty nice life. There’s amalgamated and, for lack of a better word, normal people working side by side. Shops are well-stocked, and fields are filled with delicious looking vegetables. The entire landscape is a dazzling display of vibrant colours and … oh, yeah, they have dragons.\r\n\r\nNot dragons like we had – the ones that burn villages to the ground and stomp on people for fun. No, these dragons watch over the villagers, help them with construction, farming, all sorts of stuff. They even give them this weird little thing they call a Blessing, which somehow binds them together in a way I’m seriously going to need to study later.\r\n\r\nThe people don’t worship the dragons either. There’s nothing like the goblin shenanigans down south. No, the traditional religions line up in a multifaith community with one another. Saradominists greet Zamorakians and no one starts a fight. I assume, anyway, no one really wears little badges or anything, but there are shrines to more than just Saradomin here, so I like to daydream.\r\n\r\nI set up a little shop. Can you imagine? Me, with a shop! Just selling little potions and salves, and services for those that need to speak with the dead. Simple stuff, nothing too taxing, but enough to put a roof over my head.\r\n\r\nI think I could be happy here. Well, as happy as I get.",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.3.Title": "Soot-stained Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.3.Title": "The Tale of the Ghost Wolves",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.1.Text": "The odd thing about life is it’s surprisingly easy to maintain. For all the work of alchemists and scheming sorcerers, continued existence is child’s play really. All it takes is hate.\r\n\r\nHate is a fuel that can burn forever. Pure rage is a force that can drive anyone forward. Grief is a power source that can last until the end of time. You just need to know how to use them.\r\n\r\nThere’s a morality in vengeance that society shuns. They say it won’t solve anything. That it never makes things better. Yet, I picture the suffering of those monsters and that’s all I need. Knowing they suffer, die and weep for their loved ones, that’s enough to drive my bones forward and keep the skin stitched in place.\r\n\r\nUnreasonable, yes, but at least hate is honest in it’s hypocrisy. I choose to turn the wheel of the vicious cycle round and round, grinding garou bones beneath it.\r\n\r\nI will never forgive them for the death of my friend. Never. And as long as I curse them, my soul will not fade to the world below.\r\n\r\nSomeone will tell me that that’s not what Ulv would want, but I knew my friend and, if he could speak, he’d tell me to make sure they hurt.\r\n\r\nSo, I do.\r\n\r\nThose same people tell me that grief fades, but that’s a lie. It’s been so long now, so many years, yet that pain and that hate still burn inside me more ferociously than the sun, and I wake each day smiling because I know they suffer in return.\r\n\r\nPerhaps I need a hobby?",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.7.Text": "The seals are in place, but I’m not sure what good they’ll do. A desperate attempt to try and mitigate some of the damage I’ve caused by binding Imaru to that curse. I have taken the essence of her curse and bound it to the plinths, in hope that someone stronger than me might yet claim them.\r\n\r\nDoing so will bind them to her curse in the same way that she is, but only for a while. Strong enough to challenge her. Strong enough to harm her. Without the curse she’s invulnerable, but the very same thing that makes her powerful, makes her weak.\r\n\r\nI have split them across the region, so that someone will not stumble on them by mistake. It will require dedication, focus and skill to overcome this monster of my own making, I’m sorry I cannot be the one to do it.\r\n\r\nBut, at least, I can help the one who can.",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.4.Text": "There are strange visitors to these lands, people I never expected. Unsettling, pale elves who arrive in the night and stay for an evening asking us very unusual questions. I don’t even know why we let them in. It was as if they belonged here… as if they had a right to be here.\r\n\r\nWe spoke of travel and family, of loss and of love. They asked me about the scar on my lip and the way I hold my sword at an angle. I told them about my first crush, even though I’d never shared his name with anyone.\r\n\r\nThen there was the talk of loss. Loss, like it was happening right then. A bottle spinning, fingers pointing, a choice we never chose to make. We lost someone that night, didn’t we? I don’t remember who, but there’s a hole there where a person should be. A shadow over my memories.\r\n\r\nA locked room, where no one has the key.\r\n\r\nI remember laughter, dancing and eyes like perfect rubies sparkling in the dazzling night. I remember his lips on mine, cold and tasting of metal, and then… nothing.\r\n\r\nTheir names. I don’t remember those elven names. You’d think you’d remember something like that. It’s not like we see many elves, not since that bard passed through a while ago. I feel like I should know them.\r\n\r\nBut, like all those empty rooms, somehow, I forget.",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.4.Text": "There is a crack in the heart of the world and it whispers. Smoke rises from it unlike any I’ve encountered before. There is no magma vent. No burning coal line underground. There is just emptiness softly smoking, chill as the grave.\r\n\r\nSmoke should be warm, yet this is colder than ice. A sort of strange frost that seeps into your bones. Though it strangles the air in my lungs as I stare into this fissure, I see only darkness and shadow, all the way down.\r\n\r\nThere is a power in it, unlike any I’ve seen before and I must harness it.\r\n\r\nIt started with the claw-bones of one of the failed dragon whelps. Exposed to the smoke it twitched and writhed, as if there were still muscles and sinew contracting in motion, not polished bone with no nerves attached.\r\n\r\nThere is a song in the whispering smoke. Discordant and strange. Words I don’t understand, I’m not even sure it’s language. Still, I feel a connection there, like a promise, offering me more. I am not fool enough to listen, the angler fish lure of power is all too familiar to my kind, but still perhaps I can make use of this.\r\n\r\nAfter all, one must risk everything in the pursuit of knowledge!",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonwolves.3.Text": "There once was a girl with a pet she adored.\r\nHe had fur like silver, eyes like ice.\r\nThe gentlest of natures.\r\nHe was ever so nice.\r\nBut there were things in the forest,\r\nFull of shadow and hate.\r\nWhen the girl found her friend,\r\nIt was sadly too late.\r\nEyes like glass.\r\nSkin cold as stone.\r\nThe girl wept for days.\r\nShe’d never felt more alone.\r\nSmoke rose through the woods,\r\nClawing and thick.\r\nWhen the girl breathed it in,\r\nIt made her feel sick.\r\nYet in the choking and coughing,\r\nThere whispered a voice\r\nBeautiful and terrible,\r\nAnd it gave her a choice.\r\nShe could live as she was,\r\nAlone in the night-black,\r\nOr make a pact with the smoke,\r\nAnd get her friend back.\r\nShe didn’t wait for a second.\r\nShe agreed with glee.\r\nSo the smoke told her to wait.\r\nWhere her best friend could see.\r\nEyes like embers.\r\nFur like fog.\r\nHer last words uttered.\r\n“You’re a very bad dog.”",
    "Fellhollow.Necromancer.5.Text": "Things are so much worse than I thought. The River Noumenon, the way to the Afterlife, is blocked. Imaru has somehow wedged herself in there, using the curse I gave her and her own, sheer, bloody-minded rage to stick her in place.\r\n\r\nShe claws at the edge of the Underworld, creating rifts that bleed the Noumenon’s waters into our world like some deadly poison that rips out the soul. She uses her “Blessing” as an anchor to her people, dragging their souls to her so that she might feast and grow stronger.\r\n\r\nSo focused on strength and power, on beating Kuldra, that she doesn’t think about what happens to everyone else. My soul is protected, warded by the curse that rages inside me, but the other villagers aren’t so lucky.\r\n\r\nI see tendrils of their spirits being dragged from their chests like a ragged cloak billowing in the wind. They don’t see it, of course, but they can feel it. They know something is going on and it’s leading to blind panic. The once peaceful chatter of Fellhollow is now turning to stifled screams.\r\n\r\nThis is all my fault. I need to try and find a way to fix it.",
    "Fellhollow.Zogre.2.Title": "Ulgo's Diary",
    "Fellhollow.Dragonkin.1.Text": "Viika is silent today and I don’t know if that’s a good sign. How do you relate to your sibling when they’re seeing a different “now” to you? Are they staring back at the door to our home as our parents wave them goodbye forever? Or are they enjoying tomorrow’s dinner today instead?\r\n\r\nI wish they could tell me. Share how they feel. The scientist in me would give anything to know the mind of the timeswept. The sister in me would give anything to understand my sibling.\r\n\r\nDragonkin don’t normally do family. We’re all so focused on our own problems, our constant pain, that we sometimes lack the empathy to care for someone else. Romance died the day of the curse, I swear, and family became a necessary act of survival, rather than a nurturing thing.\r\n\r\nYet I choose to defy traditional values. Viika deserves better, after all. So if they do not know what day is today, I will keep them grounded. I will be the shield against the horrors of the present, so that they will see the tomorrow they’ve already lived.\r\n\r\nAnd perhaps, if I’m lucky, they will find that special moment when their now and my now coincide together.",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.1.Title": "Weathered Diary",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.5.Title": "Weathered Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.6.Title": "Withered Diary",
    "Fellhollow.RisingDead.2.Title": "Withered Journal",
    "Fellhollow.Withering.2.Text": "You’d think they’d be cruel landlords, given that they’re dragons and all. After them beast people turned on our Southern neighbours and wiped them all out, you’d expect these dragons to do the same. They was working together after all.\r\n\r\nBut, no, that’s not how it goes. Or at least not how it’s going. The two of them kept their distance at first, pretending we weren’t here. We watched as the flight of dragons swept over us and ignored us altogether, fearing the side eyes from our two new friends.\r\n\r\nThen, when it were all over and done with, here they were. Talking to us, as though we were neighbours. Speaking to us as though we were friends.\r\n\r\nShe were… kind. There’s no other word for it. Great big blue thing made of teeth and claws, and she were singing to the children who couldn’t sleep at night. He and her, helped us build this city. Helped us find the best places to fetch water, or plant crops.\r\n\r\nHer magic brought rain and his calmed the winds, so that our harvests were plentiful, and our population bloomed. All it costs is a few sheep or cows, every once in a while, a pretty good deal if you ask me.\r\n\r\nNo gods watching over us here. No priests, nor nobles. We got dragons watching out for us, aint that a nice thing? "
  },
  "ST_FH_CollectorsCalling": {
    "Doric.CollectorsCalling.Reward.FlavourText": "A cloth shoulder back, contains useful smithing materials.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.4": "Ah don't mind me. Just a melancholic old man worried about his fully grown and perfectly capable boy. I just don't tell him enough how proud of him I am.",
    "Doric.NotStarted.QuestRejected.1": "Ah, yes, you must be quite busy. Well, I won't keep you. If you're bored later, come say hi.",
    "Doric.NotStarted.SpokenToDoric.1": "Ah, you're back. Fancy helping me find a few things?",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.GotInventorySpace.2": "Alright, last piece of the puzzle. There's this special sword that I need. Made of shadow, or smoke or something. Nasty thing, wielded by something proper wicked.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.1": "Amazing, you've got the staff! That's... that's exactly like the story... this is... hrmm. Why would this story be so accurate, unless...",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.5": "Anyway, here, have this. My little way of saying thank you for helping an old codger like me connect to happy memories.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.NotSpokenTo.3": "As the tale goes, the warrior first had to face off against a deadly archer. All bone and dark magic. Had this skeletal bow that was described in eerie detail.",
    "Objective.NecromancerStaff": "Craft a Necromancer's Staff and bring it to Doric in Fellhollow. Doric believes the recipe is in a vault somewhere.",
    "Objective.ShadowSword": "Craft a Shadow Sword and bring it to Doric in Fellhollow. Doric believes a zogre has the recipe.",
    "Objective.FindSkeletonBow": "Craft an Undead Ranger's Bow and bring it to Doric in Fellhollow. Doric believes the recipe is in a vault somewhere.",
    "Quest.Description": "Doric is looking for rare weapons in Fellhollow. ",
    "Doric.CompletedVisibleQuest.Note.Name": "Doric's Note",
    "Quest.Name": "Doric's Quest",
    "Doric.CollectorsCalling.Reward.1": "Doric's Smithing Supplies",
    "Doric.CollectorsCalling.Reward.2": "Doric's Superior Smithing Supplies",
    "Doric.InVault.Intro.GotDagger.1": "Ha, course, you already have the dagger recipe I was looking for. Shoulda guessed. Stupid Doric, never think things through.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.GotInventorySpace.GotSword.1": "Ha, of course you already have it. I never doubted you for a minute. Ok... maybe a minute, but probably no more than a few of em.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.HasSpace.1": "Here, a little something for your troubles.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.GotInventorySpace.1": "Here, my little way of saying thank you.",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.GivePotion.2": "Here, tell you what, don't tell anyone else about this momentary lapse in judgement and I'll give you something special.",
    "Doric.InVault.Intro.2": "I'd heard rumours of a special weapon here and figured, if I could get it, I could give it to Boric as a gift when I got home. Try and make up for being such a rubbish dad lately.",
    "PlayerChoice.AcceptQuest": "I'm listening",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.NotGotStaff.1": "I'm looking for a necromancer's staff. Perhaps it's another weapon in one of those dragonkin vaults?",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.DoesNotHaveBow.1": "I'm looking for an undead ranger's bow. Perhaps it's another weapon in one of those dragonkin vaults?",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.NotGotInventorySpace.1": "I've got a little something to thank you for your efforts so far, but you seem a bit overburdened. I'll hold on to it til you've got your hands a bit freer.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.NoInventorySpace.1": "I've got a little something to thank you for your efforts so far, but you seem a bit overburdened. I'll hold on to it til you've got your hands a bit freer.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.HasInventorySpace.1": "I... I'm just gonna sit here with me memories for a bit. You go on now, don't let an old git like me sour your mood. Thank you again, friend.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.HasSpace.DoesNotHaveStaff.1": "If it's anything like the bow, it'll be stored in a vault somewhere. Can you bring it to me? It'll really help with my research.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.NotSpokenTo.DoesNotHaveBow.1": "If you can find and make me that undead ranger's bow, I can compare it to the description and see if it lines up.",
    "Doric.NotStarted.Intro.2": "It may not sound like much, but sharing knowledge is what turns a gathering of people into a thriving community.",
    "Doric.InVault.Intro.NotGotDagger.1": "It seems like I overestimated these old bones and the vault guardians here did me an injury. Don't suppose you've got a potion spare I can have?",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.2": "It's all like the story. You know, I used to tell my boy this story, good old Boric. He was so excited to hear the tale of heroic warriors and undead monsters.",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.GivePotion.HasInventorySpace.2": "Kids grow up so fast. Just a few decades, that's all you have. I wish I'd spent them better.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.HasSpace.HasStaff.1": "Like that staff there! Wow, you're really good at this.",
    "PlayerChoice.RejectQuest": "Maybe later",
    "Doric.CompletedVisibleQuest.Note.Text": "My boy was always afraid of monsters, poor lad. Scared of werewolves in the cupboard and all that.   I'll find him something to keep the beasts at bay. Bring him back something to make him as proud of his old dad as his dad is of him.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.HasSpace.2": "OK, let's look at the next part of the story. There was a necromancer, nasty piece of work, with a powerful magic staff.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.DoesNotHaveInventorySpace.1": "Oh, a little overburdened I see. I'll hold onto this for you, come back and see me when you've got some space free.",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.DontGivePotion.1": "Oh, don't worry about it. I'm sure these kidneys will fix themselves up soon enough.",
    "Doric.InVault.Intro.1": "Oh, er, hello there. I appear to have gotten myself into a bit of a pickle.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.NotSpokenTo.HasBow.1": "Oh, yes, like that one you have there!",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.GivePotion.NoInventorySpace.1": "Oh, you're a bit full up there I think. Chuck something away and then we can talk.",
    "Doric.NotStarted.Intro.3": "So, what do you say to helping me out a bit more?",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.GotInventorySpace.NotGotSword.1": "So...erm... good luck? Stock up well!",
    "PlayerChoice.DontGivePotion": "Sorry [Don't Give Potion]",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.NotSpokenTo.2": "Sounds familiar, doesn't it? A land full of the undead, with deadly monsters roaming around. I'm now wondering if the story came from here somehow.",
    "Objective.SpeakToDoric": "Speak to Doric in Fellhollow.",
    "PlayerChoice.GivePotion": "Sure [Give Potion]",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.GivePotion.HasInventorySpace.1": "Thanks again for rescuing a silly old man who's still letting himself worry about his fully grown son. I guess I miss being the hero in my little boy's eyes.",
    "Doric.PostQuest": "Thanks for all your help. Ashenfall really is home to some remarkable weapons. I wonder what else we'll uncover? My boy, Boric, would love this place. ",
    "Doric.SpokenTo.GivePotion.1": "Thanks, you really a hero, don't think enough people tell you that.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.SpokenTo.HasBow.1": "That's it! That's the bow! It looks just like the story described. I wonder...",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenBow.GotStaff.GotInventorySpace.3": "The good news, is that I'm pretty sure it's not in a vault. The bad news is that I'm pretty sure it's in the possession of one of them enormous zogre thingies. You might need to kill quite a few of them to find it. ",
    "Test": "This is my first test",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.3": "To think, I'm standing in the very land this story took place. Boric would love to hear this... if... if I ever get a chance to see him again of course.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.NotGotSword.1": "We're looking for a shadow sword. When I was investigating the area the clues I found pointed to one of those zogre things. You might need to kill quite a few of them.",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.GivenStaff.GotSword.1": "Well now, there you have it! A shadow sword!",
    "Doric.QuestAccepted.NoProgress.NotSpokenTo.1": "Wonderful. Now then, I once told me lad about this strange warrior from far away. Fought great evil, undead beasties and the like.",
    "Doric.NotStarted.Intro.1": "You know what, we make a good team, you and I. You find me things and I record them for future crafters to enjoy."
  },
  "ST_FH_GhostQuest": {
    "ArtistGhost.SpokenTo.GotBook.2": "...",
    "Sketchbook.Description": "A ruined notebook, buried beneath the earth. ",
    "Zanik.Choice.Hub": "Anything I can help with?",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.4": "As the ambassador to the underworld, I feel it's my duty to help these people out. Will you help me?",
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutGhosts": "Ask about ghosts.",
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutAfterlife": "Ask about the Afterlife.",
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutTheUnderworld": "Ask about the Underworld.",
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutGhostLocations": "Ask where the ghosts are.",
    "ArtistGhost.NotGotBook.3": "But he never came back. I would have gone to look for him, but I got incinerated by a dragon. Which, you know, isn't ideal.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.GhostLocations.4": "Crumbling against decaying ruins, near a waterfall of grief, a ghost finds herself trapped with memories of a loved one. She needs something returned to her that has been buried in shadow.",
    "SketchBook.Name": "Dust-covered Sketchbook",
    "Quest.Name": "Even More Restless Ghosts",
    "GrannyGhost.NotSpokenTo.2": "Every time she visited, I would give her a clay doll. A little figurine that she could paint and display with the others, like a little village of clay friends.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Underworld.2": "Everyone just gets on with it. Similar to what it's like in the living world, only much less adventure.",
    "Objective.FindGhosts.1": "Find ghosts and complete their unfinished business. (0/3)",
    "Objective.FindGhosts.2": "Find ghosts and complete their unfinished business. (1/3)",
    "Objective.FindGhosts.3": "Find ghosts and complete their unfinished business. (2/3)",
    "Ghost.Name": "Ghost",
    "Quest.Description": "Help Zanik lay some spirits to rest by finding them and completing their unfinished business. ",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Afterlife.2": "His afterlife was, unsurprisingly, a world of constant battle. The strong crushed the weak on an endless cycle. I... I tried to protect them. I failed... a lot.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.GhostLocations.1": "I couldn't tell you where exactly, but I've got an inkling. Like an itch on the inside of my nose, pointing the way -- yeah, it's horrible, please find them.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Underworld.4": "I didn't enjoy Bandos' afterlife. I wouldn't recommend it.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Afterlife.1": "I had a bit of a god's soul in me when I died, so my afterlife didn't go very well. Bandos was, after all, pretty upset with me.",
    "VillageGhost.NotSheltered.3": "I just want four walls and a roof? Is that so much to ask? A little shelter against the cold?",
    "VillageGhost.SpokenToNotSheltered.1": "I just want four walls and a roof? Is that so much to ask? A little shelter against the cold?",
    "ArtistGhost.NotGotBook.2": "I just want to draw! Is that so much to ask? But my sketchbook is missing. My husband took it to work with him in the coal mine to the east. He likes to look at the pictures between swings.",
    "ArtistGhost.SpokenTo.NoBook.1": "I just want to draw! Is that so much to ask? But my sketchbook is missing. My husband took it to work with him in the coal mine to the east. He likes to look at the pictures between swings.",
    "ArtistGhost.NotGotBook.4": "I miss him, sure, but I really miss my sketchbook. I've had decades to get over my grief, but the boredom lasts forever!",
    "VillageGhost.NotSheltered.2": "I poured my life and soul into these foundations. Created a home for myself that I can be proud of. But now it's gone, and I feel like I'm lost without it.",
    "GrannyGhost.SpokenTo.HasDoll.DontGiveDoll.1": "I understand, hard to let go of these things. They are delightfully pretty, my granddaughter loves... no... loved them.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.GotGhostSpeak.Decline.1": "I understand. If you change your mind, or if you find one of them on your journey, please come back and see me.",
    "GrannyGhost.NotSpokenTo.3": "I wish I had one of those clay dolls to remember her by now. It would help me find peace in these turbulent times.",
    "GrannyGhost.SpokenTo.NoDoll.1": "I wish I had one of those clay dolls to remember her by now. It would help me find peace in these turbulent times.",
    "GrannyGhost.NotSpokenTo.1": "I wonder how she's doing. Whether she managed to pass on safely. My granddaughter, Edra. She used to visit me often, always a smile on her face that could warm the coldest of winters.",
    "PlayerChoice.Leave": "I'll talk to you later. ",
    "VillageGhost.Sheltered.1": "I...I...I feel warm. I feel cosy. I feel like I'm home. Thank you, thank you friend. Now I can rest and move on once the dragon has been dealt with.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Afterlife.3": "It was to be an eternity of failure. Watching the innocent slain for no reason other than some brute's entertainment. Thankfully, a friend rescued me and I got a reprieve.",
    "VillageGhost.NotSheltered.1": "It's cold, don't you feel it? The wind feels like it's rushing through me, blowing away all the years I spent building this house.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Underworld.1": "It's not as bad as it sounds, the Underworld. A bit grim, sure, but manageable. Imagine a city, full of the dead, waiting to pass on. That's what it is really.",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.GhostsFound.HasInventorySpace.1": "It's not much, I know, but I hope it helps.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Ghosts.1": "Mostly, the dead are more than happy to cross over. This world can make you weary, and it's nice to finally have an excuse to rest. But a ghost doesn't get that.",
    "ArtistGhost.SpokenTo.GotBook.1": "My sketchbook! You found it! Oh, I can't wait to draw in it again.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.GhostLocations.3": "North of here, where the world rots away from the inside, a spirit clings to the world with memories of a loved one.",
    "PlayerChoice.No": "Not right now.",
    "SketchBook.AlreadyFound": "Nothing interesting remains, just dust and old memories. ",
    "ArtistGhost.PostQuest.1": "Oh, I'm so glad to have my sketch book back. I can't wait to draw everything around me. Now... where did I put a pencil? ",
    "GrannyGhost.SpokenTo.Generic": "Oh, if only I had a little doll to remember my darling Edra by. They were such lovely decorative things, made out of clay as I recall. ",
    "ArtistGhost.SpokenTo.GotBook.3": "Oh, yeah, husband. Err... he OK? Dead you say? Into a fine paste you say? Oh dear, how tragic. I'll... err... I'll go cry now I guess?",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.GhostsFound.DoesNotHaveInventorySpace.1": "Oh, you appear to be overburdened. I'll hold onto this for you until you've got some space free.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.NoGhostspeak.1": "Oh, you'll need an amulet of ghostspeak first. I think there was one in Brynmoor, all the way back. Lost in the village somewhere. You'll need to find it.",
    "Zanik.NotSpokenTo.AlreadyStarted": "Oh, you're already looking into that? I knew I could count on you!",
    "Zanik.PostQuest.2": "Once Imaru's influence has vanished completely, the restless spirits here can rest properly.",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.GhostsFound.2": "Once all this Imaru business is dealt with, then Death will be able to help them move on properly. In the mean time, here, something to say thank you.",
    "Ghost.NoGhostspeakAmulet": "OoooOOoooOOOOOooOOOOOoooOOOh!",
    "ArtistGhost.Name": "Paint-spattered Ghost",
    "GrannyGhost.Name": "Reminiscing Ghost",
    "Objective.ReturnToZanik": "Return to Zanik.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Ghosts.3": "Some things are so important that they form a tether to our souls, that even Death's scythes can't cut. That's what a ghost is, a prisoner of ungiven closure.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Ghosts.2": "Some unfinished business keeps them trapped in place. Whether it be a mother desperately needing to know that her children are safe. Or some scholar who needs that elusive answer before they can let themselves sleep.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.3": "Still, there are some souls yet to pass on. Holding tight against Imaru's gluttony. I want to help them in these final moments, take the burdens from them so they can pass on once the dragon's power has fully waned.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.1": "Strange place this, isn't it? Not just the zombies and the horrible red pools of awfulness, there's a sadness to it too. A misery, like a chasm stretching across everything.",
    "Objective.FindZanikNotSpokenYet": "Tell someone about these spirits. ",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.SomeGhostsFound.1": "Thank you for helping some of the spirits, but there are more still that need help finding peace. Please keep searching.",
    "VillageGhost.PostQuestNoLongerSheltered.1": "Thank you for the shelter, even if it was short-lived. It was nice to be out of the cold, even for a little while. ",
    "VillageGhost.Sheltered.2": "Thank you!",
    "Zanik.PostQuest.1": "Thank you, I can feel them at peace, it's beautiful. The dead can get trapped in their issues, locked into a vicious cycle. You've stopped that.",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.GhostsFound.1": "Thank you, I can feel them at peace, it's beautiful. The dead can get trapped in their issues, locked into a vicious cycle. You've stopped that.",
    "GrannyGhost.PostQuest.1": "Thank you, again. I just know that Edra would have loved it.",
    "GrannyGhost.SpokenTo.HasDoll.GiveDoll.1": "Thank you. Thank you so much. I can rest now. Well... once the devouring force has gone at least. Thank you again, my friend. You have made this old fool very happy.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.GotGhostSpeak.AcceptQuest.1": "Thank you. There are three lost souls all over Fellhollow, hidden in the remnants of human civilisation. I feel them, like a warm fire in this cold dark place.",
    "GrannyGhost.SpokenTo.HasDoll.1": "That doll! That clay figurine! It's just like the ones I made for my granddaughter. Would... would you be so kind as to give it to me? It would help me find peace.",
    "ArtistGhost.NotGotBook.1": "The afterlife is so dull, they don't tell you that in the books. Endless sameyness. Nothing changes. I want to yawn and yawn, but I can't even do that. No breath you see.",
    "Zanik.QuestNotStarted.Intro.2": "The dead don't pass on here, not really. The tethers that hold them to their bodies are stretched and snap against Imaru's hunger. Then they're devoured like evening snacks.",
    "Zanik.QuestStarted.NoGhosts.1": "There are three lost souls all over Fellhollow, hidden in the remnants of human civilisation. Each one has something stopping them from finding peace.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.Underworld.3": "There's a great big river, the river Noumenon, that you can sail down on to whatever afterlife waits for you -- yeah, there's more than one. Each depending on your own beliefs. Or, if you're unlucky enough to be like me, the belief of the god's soul that's infected you.",
    "Zanik.AskAbout.GhostLocations.2": "There's a village, long since fallen to ruin. There waits a spirit shivering against the wind and rain.",
    "VillageGhost.Name": "Windswept Ghost",
    "PlayerChoice.Yes": "Yes.",
    "SketchBook.AlreadyFound.NotFinished": "You already have this. You should return it to its owner. ",
    "SketchBook.NotCollected.Space": "You find an old sketchbook. ",
    "SketchBook.NotCollected.NoSpace": "You find and old sketchbook, but your inventory is too full to collect it. ",
    "PlayerChoice.DontGiveDecoration": "[Don't give the ghost a clay decoration.]",
    "PlayerChoice.GiveDecoration": "[Give the ghost a clay decoration.]"
  },
  "ST_FH_SpiritChinchompa": {
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutNatureSpirits": "Ask about nature spirits.",
    "PlayerChoice.AskAboutChinchompas": "Ask about spectral chinchompas.",
    "Vannaka.WildHuntCompleted.NotSpokenTo.Intro.3": "Chinchompas. Ghostly little critters with explosive personalities. They threaten our efforts here, as the land does not understand we work in its interest.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.SpokenTo.NoProgress.1": "Find those chinchompa spirits and put an end to them before they can put an end to you. If they explode, their essence will just reform somewhere else, so strike them before they can.",
    "Objective.GatherSkulls": "Gather 10 spectral chinchompa skulls and bring them to Vannaka in Fellhollow.",
    "Quest.Description": "Gather spectral chinchompa skulls so that Vannaka can help the land heal. ",
    "Vannaka.GotHeads.1": "Good, that looks like enough of their skulls to send a message. I'm not good with magic, but there are old rituals, primal and primordial, that the land will listen to.",
    "Vannaka.GenericGreeting": "Hello there, young pup, what can I help you with?",
    "Vannaka.GotHeads.InventoryFree.1": "Here, something for your hard work. It's not much, young pup, but it'll be a reminder of the good work you've done for this place.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotSpokenToVannaka.GotSkulls.1": "Hrmm, what do you have there young pup? The spectral skulls of vengeful little spirits? I know what this means.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotSpokenToVannaka.NotAllSkulls.1": "Hrmm, what do you have there young pup? The spectral skulls of vengeful little spirits? I know what this means.",
    "Vannaka.QuestComplete.HasMoreSkulls.1": "I see you've been hunting more of those spiritual pests. Nasty creatures those, best to get rid of them. Here, I'll take those skulls off your hands and give you something for your efforts. ",
    "Vannaka.GotHeads.NoInventoryFree.1": "I've got something for you, a thank you of sorts, but you're a little overburdened. Clear out some of that backpack and then come back and see me.",
    "Vannaka.WildHuntCompleted.NotSpokenTo.Intro.5": "If you bring me ten of their skulls, I can do what I can to help lay their spirits to rest. Perhaps we can curb some of this land's fury.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.SpokenTo.NoProgress.2": "If you bring me their skulls, I can do what I can to help lay their spirits to rest. Perhaps we can curb some of this land's fury.",
    "Vannaka.QuestComplete.HasMoreSkulls.Finish.1": "If you find more of them, bring them to me. I'll take ten at a time, clear the problem up faster that way. ",
    "Vannaka.GotHeads.2": "In time, thanks to this, and with Imaru's destruction, we may see the land return to the lush land it once was. In a few decades perhaps.",
    "Vannaka.WildHuntCompleted.NotSpokenTo.Intro.4": "It is the vet's hand that the dog bites most, after all. I need you to find these critters and hunt down as many as you can, before they explode and rip the land apart in the process.",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.1": "It'll take some time for the land to heal, but when it does it'll remember the good work you've done for it. The land always remembers.",
    "Vannaka.QuestComplete.HasSkulls.NoSpace.1": "Or I would, if you weren't so overburdened. Clear some space, young pup, then come find me. ",
    "Objective.SpeakToVannaka": "Speak to Vannaka in Fellhollow.",
    "Vannaka.WildHuntCompleted.NotSpokenTo.Intro.2": "The land is angry. Enraged at the corruption forced upon it and in turn it fights back. Dangerous spirits of destruction roam this land in the fluffiest of forms.",
    "Quest.Name": "Things That Go Boom In The Night",
    "Vannaka.LinkFromWitherBeast.1": "You've earned a rest, but if you're looking for work come back and see me. I have another task I could use your help with. ",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotSpokenToVannaka.GotSkulls.2": "You've got enough there for me to sort this mess out. An old ritual, primal and primordial nonsense -- not my favourite thing to work with, but needs must.",
    "Vannaka.WildHuntCompleted.NotSpokenTo.Intro.1": "Young pup, it seems like the spirits here are in dire trouble and I'll need a little more of your help to put things right."
  },
  "ST_FH_WitherBeast": {
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.LessThanThreeHearts.2": "Ah, but I see you've been liberating more nature spirits. Good work. It may feel strange, but you're doing them a favour, trust me. Tell you what, bring me three of them and I'll give you some of those shiny stones Death seems so interested in.",
    "Vannaka.NoInventorySpace": "Ah, or I would give them to you if you had any room. Make some space and then come back and talk to me. ",
    "Vannaka.NotStarted.GatheredAllThreeHearts.1": "Ah... but your a skilled hunter, young pup, I see you've already gathered them.",
    "Objective.BringHeartNotStarted": "Bring the Primordial Heart to someone with an interest in the wild hunt. ",
    "Objective.BringHeart": "Bring the hearts to Vannaka. ",
    "Vannaka.Intro.4": "Don't worry, they're meant to be hunted. That's the spirit way, a spirit of nature should be hunted by a predator, not slowly drained away by a monster, and you're the apex predator here.",
    "Vannaka.Intro.2": "Even this willow grove, once home to a proud and magnificent nature spirit, is now corrupted by wither and rot. That poor spirit has withered away to nothing.",
    "Quest.Description": "Help Vannaka safeguard Fellhollow's nature spirits, by hunting them down, in willow groves, and collecting their hearts. ",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.NoHearts.1": "How are you and your new friend getting on? Running wild and free, I hope. See, you did them a favour by hunting them here. Now they're safe from this land's blighted curse.",
    "Objective.HuntBeast": "Hunt down Nature Spirits near Fellhollow's willow groves and bring three of their hearts to Vannaka. ",
    "Vannaka.NotStarted.GatheredAtLeastOneHeart.1": "I see you're part way there already. Just need to get the rest and we can help this spirit escape Imaru's foul curse.",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.GotHearts.3": "I'll take them off your hands and you can take these in their place. Shiny little stones that old Harold loves so much.",
    "Vannaka.Intro.3": "If this land is ever going to heal, we need to save the rest of those spirits and the only way to save them, is to hunt them and kill them.",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.Info.1": "If you find another three hearts on your travels, bring them to me and I'll exchange them for some of those shiny soul fragments that Harold seems so fond of. ",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.GotHearts.2": "It's a way to liberate the spirit from this place. Allow it to run free and wild, bound to a new anchor, one able to give them freedom.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotProgressed.1": "Look for willow groves, like this one, those are places where nature spirits thrive. There's a few to the west of here. Bring me three of their hearts and we can find a way to keep them safe from this withering hunger.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotGotHearts.2": "Look for willow groves, those are places where nature spirits thrive. There's a few to the west of here. Bring me the spirits' hearts and we can find a way to keep them safe from this withering hunger.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.NotGotHearts.1": "Majestic creatures, aren't they? I'm sure it feels strange to have to hunt them, but trust me we're doing them a favour. You're part way there, but I'll need more hearts.",
    "Vannaka.Intro.1": "Not a pleasant landscape this, ey, young pup? Life is fading, drained away by a dragon's hunger. Rotten creatures, dragons.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.GotHearts.3": "That anchor is you. Now, one moment and... here... that should do it. With a little magic, that spirit will carry you across Ashenfall. Give it a good run, won't you?",
    "Quest.Name": "The Wild Hunt",
    "Vannaka.Name": "Vannaka",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.GotHearts.1": "You and your spirit friend seem happy together, young pup. Always good to see that sort of bond between man and beast.",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.LessThanThreeHearts.1": "You and your spirit friend seem happy together, young pup. Always good to see that sort of bond between man and beast.",
    "Vannaka.QuestStarted.GotHearts.1": "You did it, well done. Now, the tricky part. I asked you to get these hearts because of a garou ritual I learned. An old one, from their time before Kuldra.",
    "Vannaka.Intro.5": "You'll be doing this place a favour by hunting them, trust me. Look for willow groves, like this one, those are places where nature spirits thrive. Bring me three of their hearts and we can find a way to keep them safe from this withering hunger.",
    "Vannaka.PostQuest.GotHearts.2": "You've gathered another three hearts for me from the nature spirits? Good, very good. You're a skilled hunter, young pup, you should be proud."
  },
  "ST_FH_WitherWard": {
    "Crystal.Description": "A crystal that Doric obtained from a cave near the river Salve, back in Misthalin. Used in creating the Salve amulet. ",
    "Objective.FindRecipe": "Access the vault and find the hidden secret within. ",
    "Objective.ReturnToDoric": "Bring the dwarven writing to Doric. ",
    "Doric.Name": "Doric",
    "Objective.LookForDoric": "Find someone in Fellhollow that can translate dwarvish text. ",
    "Quest.Description": "Find the statues to gain entrance to the vault and uncover the secrets that lie within. ",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.HasInventorySpace.1": "Hope it helps in your travels.",
    "Doric.PostQuest.1": "Hope that amulet helps you out. There are a lot of them shamblin'orribles out there and anything to keep 'em off you feels like a good thing. ",
    "Doric.Intro.1": "I don't like this place, it's creepy and weird. Had to whack several zombies with my hammer and now it's got this weird purple ooze on it that won't wash off.",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.2": "I guess we'll never know. Here, let me translate this for you, hopefully it'll help you on your travels.",
    "Doric.QuestStarted.NoProgress.2": "If you can find your way inside, let me know if you discover anything interesting.",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.4": "Oh! Ha, you're gonna laugh at this, but I actually have one of them river Salve gemstones. I found one a few years back and I just keep it with me as a good luck charm. Here, you should take it, make yourself one of those salve amulets.",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.DoesNotHaveInventorySpace.1": "Oh, you don't appear to have the space for it. Come back and see me when you do.",
    "Crystal.Name": "Salve Crystal",
    "Quest.Name": "Seeking Salvation",
    "Doric.Intro.2": "Still, I'm betting there's something interesting waiting around here. There are vaults in this place and they must be loaded with dragonkin secrets.",
    "Doric.QuestStarted.NoProgress.1": "Taken a look in that locked vault yet? There must be a trick to it. Those dragonkin were a smart lot, secretive... and arrogant as heck.",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.3": "Well now, that is unexpected. This is the Salve amulet... why is this here? It requires a gemstone only found by the river Salve back in Misthalin. I mean, it's handy against the undead, so it'll be real useful here.",
    "Doric.FoundStatue.1": "Well, will you look at that, another dwarven tablet. Why were the dragonkin out here stealing dwarven secrets?",
    "Doric.Intro.3": "Who knows what you might find? I discovered one vault, and I was all geared up to visit, but it's locked down tight. Hey, I know, if you get a chance why don't you take a look? Let me know what you find inside.",
    "Statue.Discover.1": "You find strange dwarven writings that you cannot read. Perhaps Doric can translate for you.",
    "Statue.Discover.NotStarted.1": "You find strange dwarven writings that you cannot read. Perhaps someone can translate for you.",
    "Door.SealBroken": "You hear the sound of a dragonkin lock releasing. "
  },
  "ST_FTUE": {
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro5": "A bit of damage to your soul. Don't worry, it's not permanent, but perhaps avoid overindulging in Wardstones, eh?",
    "WoM_SkippedTutorial_IKnowYou_1": "A lifetime of heroism, and no recognition. But you rob one bank, and suddenly everyone knows your name!",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_Intro1": "A new adventure is always exciting, don't you think? We lost some good people... friends... but we need to push forward, in their memory.",
    "Zanik_RM_Intro4": "About fifty ash logs should do it, so make sure you've got a well maintained axe. Shouldn't take too long, come back to me when you have them.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_GotWater1": "Ah good, you've got some water. Bit dirty, I know, but better than nothing. Be careful though, the water's tainted and it'll make life difficult if you drink too much.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro1": "Ah, I see you've discovered Ashenfall's little \"blacksmith benefit\", as I like to call it. Lifeward!",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_AlreadyGotWater1": "Ah, but you've got a good head on yer shoulders. I see you've already got some water, so you won't die of thirst. ",
    "Doric_RTftJ_GotCleanWater1": "Ah, good, you've got some nice clean water there. The water in lakes and rivers tends to be dirty, tainted by something nasty that will make life difficult if you drink too much. ",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Wardstone_Choice_01": "Ah, hello. What would you like to discuss?",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_MadeStone1": "Ah, you've made one. Lovely. See, that barely hurt at all. Just a little drop of blood, nothing to cry about. But now, when your lifeward is damaged, you can repair it.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro2": "And look at ya! Not a knife to yer name, no, no, we can't be doing with that. Come on, let's get you prepared. You need to go and craft a stone club.",
    "WoM_Generic": "Aren't you helping the others out? What are you talking to me for? Check your map if you're not sure what you're meant to be doing.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_3": "As well as goblins, look at the creatures here. So vibrant and full of life. This whole place feels... magical.",
    "WS_Playerchoice_Askabout_Wardstone": "Ask about Lifeward.",
    "WS_Playerchoice_Askabout_DragonSlayer": "Ask about the Dragon Slayer quest. ",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs3": "Axtral projection will let you slice down trees with a wave of your fingers. Much less time consuming than the lumberjack gig.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_MadeClub1": "Aye, that's a fine club you got there, but even the best weapons break over time. When that happens use a crafting bench to repair your gear.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_1": "Be ready to fight, that's my first piece of advice. Craft armour, weapons and anything else you need for battle.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_MadeClub2": "Before you go, here, something to help you on your way.",
    "FS_Description": "Begin your adventure.",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro3": "Behind me, up that little hill, is a windmill infested with rats. I want you to kill some of them and cook their meat.",
    "Zanik_RM_LinkToWoM2": "Better not keep him waiting too long, he gets real cranky. ",
    "Doric_RTftJ_NotMadeClub2": "Both require stone and ash logs, which you'll find scattered all over the ground around here.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Objective3": "Bring your Small Wardstone to the Wise Old Man.",
    "WoM_FS_Intro3": "But before all that, how about we take you through some survival basics?",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_WaterNeeded1": "But look at you, all skin and bones. Must be proper parched after a journey like that.",
    "WoM_FS_SkippedTutorial2": "But not here. Come find me in Bramblemead Village, and we'll get you started.",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_2": "But you see that great tower, off in the distance? That's dragonkin that is. Means there's probably stuff worth finding about this place.",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs4": "But, magic comes at a cost -- runes. You'll need both air and astral runes to cast Axtral projection, so here's how to get them.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro1": "By Saradomin's big bushy beard! Just our luck, a great ruddy dragon. Think it were him that got the others - may they rest in peace.",
    "WoM_Skipped_Tutorial_1": "Can I help you?",
    "Playerchoice_TellMeAboutAshenfall": "Can you tell me about Ashenfall?",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Objective2": "Craft a Small Wardstone at a Rune Altar and bring it to the Wise Old Man.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro2": "Crafting certain equipment intrinsically involves the weaving of small threads of enchantment, granting you greater protection.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_2": "Cull the population of monsters, to make the world a better place.",
    "Zanik_RM_SpokenTo_NoLogs": "Cut down trees and gather 50 ash logs, then bring them to me.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_WaterNeeded2": "Dehydration and starvation are deadlier than dragons, so you're going to need keep an eye on your basic needs, like hunger and thirst.",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro4": "Don't pull that face, you can't be a picky eater in a place like this. Food will make you healthier and heartier, and much more likely to survive.",
    "RTftJ_Description": "Doric wants to teach you some survival basics. ",
    "Zanik_RM_Intro1": "Dragons, it had to be dragons. Oh, hi, sorry, nice to meet you, I'm Zanik. I'm the local survival and goblin expert around here.",
    "WoM_FS_SkippedTutorial1": "Fair enough, I do like someone that can show initiative.",
    "FS_Title": "First Steps",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs2": "Fortunately, we've got magic! As you improve in a skill you'll discover spells that you can use, such as my favourite - Axtral Projection.",
    "Doric_Generic": "Gathering resources and crafting items, that's the basics of survival in this place. Seek out new resources to discover new recipes.",
    "RTftJ_Title": "Getting Started",
    "Vannaka_RC_NotDoneRTftJ": "Getting ahead of yourself, aren't we, young pup? Check your map to see where you're meant to be headed. ",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_NotMadeStone": "Go and craft a wardstone and bring it here so I can check your working. You just need to gather some rune essence and stone, and craft them at a rune altar. Nice and simple. One wardstone will do.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro6": "Go and craft me one small wardstone and bring it here so I can check your working. You just need to gather some rune essence and stone, and craft it at a rune altar. Nice and simple. One small wardstone will do.",
    "Zanik_RM_HasRunes1": "Great work! Runes are the lifeblood of magic, you'll need them to cast spells and use magic staves. A well placed spell can make all the difference.",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs1": "Great, you've got them. Now, between you and me, that was a bit repetitive right? I'd be exhausted having to do that all the time.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro3": "Handy stuff, especially with dragons about. Now, you'll find that your Lifewards can get depleted by the brutality of the other creatures on Ashenfall.",
    "WoM_FS_AcceptedTutorial3": "He's the only dwarf on the continent, that we know of anyway, can't miss him.",
    "Zanik_RM_Intro3": "Here, I'll show you. First, let's look at things without magic to help you. I need you to cut down a couple of trees and bring me some ash logs. Simple, right?",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_NoInventorySpace": "Hrmm, I have something for you, but it appears you've overloaded yourself like a magpie gone mad. Clear some space, then come and see me.",
    "Vannaka_NoRoomInInventory": "Hrmm, seems you're carrying the weight of the world right now. Come see me again when you've got some space free in your backpack. ",
    "WoM_Generic_Hrmm": "Hrmm?",
    "Player_Choice_FS_SkipTutorial": "I can work it out [Skip Tutorial]",
    "Playerchoice_IKnowYou": "I recognise you from the wanted posters!",
    "Zanik_NotDoneRTftJ": "I think someone is looking for you. Mentioned a task they needed you to complete. Check your map for where to find them. ",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_3": "I was finding things a little stale on the mainland. When I saw the posters for the expedition, I felt a pull... a call to adventure that I could not resist.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_2": "I wonder why they're not in the history books.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_1": "I'm Zanik, I'm a cave goblin. Sort of like the goblins over there in Bramblemead village... only we chose a peace over violence.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_3": "I'm regretting it a bit, what with big scary dragons and all, but I'm excited too. Looking forward to learn everything about this place.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_WaterNeeded3": "I've marked two ponds on your map, to the northwest and south of us. Grab some water from there and bring it back here. Then I'll teach you what you'll need to survive.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_WaterNeeded4": "If you see a redberry bush along the way, grab yourself a handful. Not much of a meal, but a little food is better than no food at all.",
    "Vannaka_RC_HasKebabs2": "It may not exactly be gourmet cooking, but a meal like this could make the difference between life and death. You'll not be taking on any dragons if you're starving to death. ",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro3": "It won't kill a dragon, but it's better than nothing and it'll help you live a bit longer, giving you time to make something better.",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_1": "It's a wild place this. Beasties everywhere, and no civilisation in sight. Just the remnants, ghosts of the past.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_MadeStone3": "Just don't use too many at once, and you'll be fine. Right, go on, get out there and slay that dragon!",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_MadeStone2": "Just use a wardstone and BAM! Instant Lifeward recharge. Sure, it'll tear a bit out of your soul, but so will listening to Doric talk about hammers for three hours.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_Intro_1": "Keep your wits about you, young pup. Ashenfall is home to many a dangerous beast, and I've not yet tested my blade against each of them.",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_2": "Left my son behind to watch the shop. Good lad, gonna do good things. Hope he's not too worried about his dad.",
    "Vannaka_Generic": "Life on Ashenfall is rarely peaceful. Make sure you're well fed and always have a weapon to hand. Keep an eye on enemy weaknesses to dispatch them quickly. ",
    "LO_Title": "Log On",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro2": "Look, you may have a weapon, but every great warrior knows wars are won by the stomach, not the blade.",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_1": "Me? Name's Doric. I'm just a stupid old blacksmith that got swept up in tales of adventure. Trying to win back me glory days.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_2": "Most of my people stay underground, hiding from the surface. But I couldn't wait to explore this vast and wonderful world.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_1": "My name is Vannaka and back on the mainland I was a Slayer Master. It was my job to send adventurers after dangerous beasts.",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs_NoRunes": "Not made the runes yet? You'll need to mine essence from the floating geysers and then craft air and astral runes on a rune altar.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_NextStep": "Now you've got something to fight with, go chat to Vannaka over to the north east, he can teach you how to keep fighting fit.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_MadeDagger2": "Now, even the best weapons break over time. When that happens use a crafting bench to repair your gear.",
    "Doric_SkippedWom": "Oh dear, you just walked right past the Wise Old Man. He won't like that. Best go back and say hi, eh?",
    "Doric_NoRoomInInventory": "Oh dear, you seem a little overburdened at the moment. Come and see me when you've got some space free in your backpack. ",
    "Zanik_NoRoomInInventory": "Oh wow, bit of a packrat are we? You're carrying too much right now, come back and chat with me when you've cleared some space from your backpack. ",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro5": "Oh, I'm Doric by the way. Resident blacksmith and craftsperson on this expedition. Nice to meet you. Now, stop standing around and go make that club!",
    "WoM_FS_DragonSlayer_Started": "Oh, don't mind me here. I'm just enjoying the architecture. I'll meet you at Bramblemead Village if you want to chat. ",
    "WoM_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_1": "Oh, the cruelty of time, erasing even our deeds. I was once a famous and adored hero. Now everyone just calls me \"that wise old man\". Rude really.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_MadeDagger1": "Oh, you made a dagger, not a club? Aye, it's a nice piece of work, not what I asked for, but that's fine.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_3": "Past Bramblemead is Ghornfell, a place of danger and excitement. Something calls to me out there and I intend to seek it out.",
    "WoM_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_3": "Probably goes someway to explaining the enormous dragon that wants to kill us... along with all the other things that want to kill us.",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro5": "Properly cook a rat roast and bring them back to me. You'll probably burn a few along the way, don't let that disuade you. No one said survival would be pretty.",
    "RC_Title": "Ratcatcher",
    "Vannaka_RC_HasKebabs4": "Rats, for example, don't take kindly to getting stabbed. Here, take this little butterknife to make it easier to fight them in future. You can have this as well, it'll help you with what's next.",
    "Vannaka_RC_HasKebabs5": "Right, let's teach you a bit about magic. Zanik's the one to talk to for that, you can find her down the road just before the river.",
    "Zanik_RM_LinkToWoM1": "Right, now that you've learned the basics, it's time to get started. The Wise Old Man is waiting for you just outside Bramblemead Village. Follow your compass to find him.",
    "RM_Title": "Rune Mysteries",
    "Zanik_RM_HasLogs5": "See those geysers around, with the floating rocks? Take this pickaxe and mine some essence from them, build a rune altar and then craft the runes from rune essence.",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Objective1": "Speak to the Wise Old Man to learn about Lifewards.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro_AlreadyGotWater2": "Still, it's going to be tough surviving this place with a dragon about. ",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_WhoAreYou_3": "Still, no point lollygagging around. I'll catch my breath and then explore these new lands. Who knows? Might find something.",
    "Doric_SkippedTutorial_Intro_1": "Strange place this. Ashenfall, I mean. Could make a real home here, if things stopped trying to kill us.",
    "WS_QuestDesc": "The Wise Old Man wants to teach you about Lifewards and how to recharge them.",
    "Zanik_RM_Intro2": "The interesting thing about Ashenfall is that it's laced with magic. Anima everywhere, pouring out of the ground. Which we can use to our advantage.",
    "WoM_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_2": "The whole continent feels like its infused with anima. Literally pouring out of the ground in some places. That's just not normal.",
    "Vannaka_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_2": "There are goblins everywhere in Bramblemead and deadlier things beyond.",
    "Zanik_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_1": "There are goblins here, that's unexpected. I thought I knew about all the tribes, but there's a whole load of them here.",
    "Zanik_Generic": "There are secrets hidden all over Ashenfall, I'm sure of it. Look around, explore, and see what you can find. ",
    "WS_WiseOldMan_Intro4": "To recharge them, you'll need to craft yourself wardstones. These impressive little doohickies will recharge the Lifeward enchantments on your armour... at a small cost.",
    "RC_Description": "Vannaka wants to teach you the basics of hunting, fighting and cooking. ",
    "Zanik_NotDoneRC": "Vannaka was looking for you, mentioned something about fine dining?",
    "WS_QuestName": "Warding Off Danger",
    "WoM_SkippedTutorial_CanYouTellMeAboutAshenfall_1": "We've not been here that long, but I can tell you that Ashenfall is special. You must feel it? Magic everywhere?",
    "WoM_FS_Intro1": "Welcome to Ashenfall, sorry about the mess. Had a bit of a dragon problem, that's why we've called for you.",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro_Dagger": "Well met, young pup. Looking to get yourself ready to face off against a dragon? You'll need more than that butter knife to kill one, but you've got to start somewhere.",
    "Vannaka_RC_Intro1": "Well met, young pup. Looking to get yourself ready to face off against a dragon? You'll need more than that potato masher to kill one, but you've got to start somewhere.",
    "Vannaka_RC_NoProgress1": "Well met, young pup. Seems like you haven't managed to cook that rat roast for me yet. You can get them by killing giant rats and cooking their meat. You can find some up by the windmill. ",
    "Vannaka_RC_HasKebabs1": "Well met, young pup. Seems your hunt was successful, I see you've gathered the food I asked for.",
    "Playerchoice_WhoAreYou": "Who are you?",
    "Player_Choice_FS_AcceptTutorial": "Yes please [Begin Tutorial]",
    "Vannaka_RC_HasKebabs3": "You will find rats are annoyingly resilient to clubs. Some enemies can resist certain damage types and be vulnerable to others.",
    "WoM_FS_AcceptedTutorial2": "You'll find him outside the temple. Check your map if you get lost, but he should be easy to spot.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_Intro4": "You'll need to gather stone and ash logs, which you can find laying around, then you'll want to build a crafting table to craft the club.",
    "Zanik_RM_HasRunes2": "You'll unlock new spells as you improve your skills. Here, this book should help you toward that. Have a play around with them, you'll find they can be incredibly useful.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_NotMadeClub1": "You'll want to build yourself a crafting table. Then once you've done that craft yourself a stone club.",
    "WoM_FS_AcceptedTutorial1": "You'll want to get to grips with gathering and crafting first, Doric can help you with that.",
    "WoM_FS_Intro2": "You've come at a great time. Heroic opportunities await. This long-forgotten place is just screaming to be explored.",
    "Doric_RTftJ_GotWater2": "Zanik says boiling it sorts it all out. So might want to give that a look later, when you've got a chance. Anyway, time we got you all set up to survive this harsh land.",
    "LO_Description": "Zanik wants to teach you the basics of woodcutting.",
    "RM_Description": "Zanik wants you to learn the basics of crafting runes."
  },
  "ST_FTUE_Farming": {
    "FlavourText_FinishedFarmingTutorialPack": "A cloth bag with some useful items for farmers.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.IntroReturn": "Anything else I can help you with?",
    "WS_PlayerChoice_AskAboutFarming": "Ask about Farming",
    "PlayerChoice.QuestionHub.AskAboutCompost": "Ask about compost.",
    "PlayerChoice.QuestionHub.AskAboutSeeds": "Ask about planting seeds.",
    "PlayerChoice.QuestionHub.AskAboutWatering": "Ask about watering plants. ",
    "Name_FarmingTutorialPack": "Bag of Seeds",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Compost.1": "Compost improves the yield on your crops when you harvest them. They simply love to spread their roots around in the stinky stuff.",
    "FlavourText_FarmingTutorialPack": "Contains different types of seeds from brynmoor.",
    "FarmingRewardItem": "Farming Reward Pack",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.PlantingSeeds.1": "First, you'll need to build a farming plot. Use a spade on it to clear it of weeds. Once it's completely clear, you're ready to plant.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Compost.3": "Give it a little time for the newly added stuff to rot down into compost and then take a Compost Bucket and fill it up.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Watering.2": "Grab yourself a watering can, fill it with water at a water source, and then liberally douse your patch until it's fully soaked through.",
    "Objective.HarvestCrop": "Grow and harvest your first crop from a farming plot. ",
    "Quest.Name": "Growing Pains",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Intro.4": "Here, take these to get you started.",
    "PlayerChoice.QuestionHub.Leave": "I have no more questions. ",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Intro.1": "I see you've started to get a little green around the thumbs! Farming will make survival on Ashenfall a little less horrible.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.PlantingSeeds.2": "Just grab the seeds in your hand, and then whack em into the soil. No need for grace, or ceremony, just whomp them in and they'll be fine.",
    "Quest.Description": "Learn the basics of the Farming skill from the Wise Old Man. ",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Finished.1": "Look at you, practically master farmer already. Farming is a wonderful way to keep yourself well fed, and with access to useful materials.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Watering.3": "Make sure to water your plants every day, ideally first thing in the morning, to keep them nice and healthy.",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.NoInventorySpace": "Oh? You've overburdened yourself with all the random things you can cram in your pockets. Come back and see me when you've made a bit of room.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Watering.1": "Plants are like people, they need water to survive. You'll want to keep your plants nice and hydrated, so that they don't succumb to disease.",
    "Objective.FinishQuest": "Return to the Wise Old Man in Bramblemead.",
    "Name_FinishedFarmingTutorialPack": "Spare Farmers Supplies",
    "Objective.SpeakToWOM1": "Speak to the Wise Old Man, in Bramblemead, to learn about the Farming skill. ",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Finished.2": "Speaking of useful, here, take this. My little gift to you. Just don't tell the others, they'll get all jealous again.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Compost.4": "Then just pour the contents of your bucket over the farming plot, making sure it's spread over it as fully as possible.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.Compost.2": "To make compost, you'll first need to build a Compost Bin. Then you'll want to fill it with compostible ingredients, like weeds, unwanted logs or irritating exes.",
    "WoM.QuestionHub.IntroFirstTime": "What would you like to know?",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Intro.3": "Why don't you go and give it a proper go right now? Go harvest some crops and then come back and see me. I'll give you a little something for your efforts.",
    "WoM.TalkAboutFarming.Intro.2": "You'll be able to grow fruits, vegetables, and all manner of plants. Food, potion ingredients and perhaps some crafting resources too!"
  },
  "ST_FTUENotifications": {
    "UI.FTUE.DodgeBlockAndParryControls": "1. {BlockButton} to block.\r\n2. {EvadeButton} to dodge.\r\n3. Blocking an enemy attack at the right moment will parry an enemy attack.\r\n4. Enemies that have been parried take more damage.",
    "UI.FTUE.BedsText": "A bed will let you rest and gives you somewhere to recover if you're too badly hurt. ",
    "UI.FTUE.StealthArcheryText": "A bow is great for taking our targets from the shadows. Try sneaking to make it harder for others to spot you. ",
    "UI.FTUE.ProcessingFuelText": "A good fire is a great way to keep warm, but you'll need to keep it burning. A steady supply of kindling stops it from burning out. ",
    "UI.FTUE.NeedStrongerAxeTitle": "Acquiring better tools",
    "UI.FTUE.BuildingBeamsText": "Adding support beams to your building will improve stability.",
    "UI.FTUE.FriendlyCharacters": "Approach friendly characters to speak with them.",
    "UI.FTUE.RespawningLocationBed": "As you have claimed a bed you'll return there, otherwise you'll be taken to the temple. ",
    "UI.FTUE.DurabilityDropText": "As you use tools, armour and weapons, they will fall into disrepair as their durability falls. When something has no durability left it becomes broken.",
    "UI.FTUE.BetterGearText": "As you venture further you will come across new materials which will unlock new recipes. Crafting better equipment will increase your chances of survival.",
    "UI.FTUE.ExploreText": "Ashenfall is home to many useful resources, exploration will give you access to different materials.",
    "UI.FTUE.FatigueText": "Avoid exhaustion by getting a good night's sleep, if you're too tired you'll find exploring much more difficult. ",
    "UI.FTUE.BackpackTitle": "Backpack",
    "UI.FTUE.BuildingBeamsTitle": "Beams",
    "UI.FTUE.BedsTitle": "Beds",
    "UI.FTUE.BetterGearTitle": "Better gear",
    "UI.FTUE.StealthArcheryTitle": "Bows and Sneaking",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Placement.Title": "Building",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Unlocked.2.Title": "Building",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessSkills": "Certain actions will award you XP in one of several skills. As you gain XP your skills will gain levels which will give you access to new features and powerful spells.",
    "UI.FTUE.FirstNightTitle": "Cold",
    "UI.FTUE.CombatVsGoblinsTitle": "Combat",
    "UI.FTUE.Cooking.Title": "Cooking",
    "UI.FTUE.CraftingItems.Title": "Crafting Items",
    "UI.FTUE.CraftingItems.Text": "Crafting benches allow you to create tools and other items.",
    "UI.FTUE.DurabilityDropTitle": "Durability",
    "UI.FTUE.FoodBenenfitsText": "Eating food provides Sustenance, which improves health regeneration.",
    "UI.FTUE.FirstArmorEquip.Text2": "Enemy power levels are indicated next to their health bar. The higher the power level, the more dangerous the foe. Make sure you are properly equipped to face them.",
    "UI.FTUE.FatigueTitle": "Exhaustion",
    "UI.FTUE.ExploreTitle": "Explore",
    "UI.FTUE.FoodBenefitsTitle": "Food Benefits",
    "UI.FTUE.ProcessingFuelTitle": "Fuel",
    "UI.FTUE.CombatVsGoblinsText": "Goblins? Aggressive critters. Keep your wits about you, damage avoided is better than damage blocked. Choose your attacks carefully. ",
    "UI.FTUE.HealthRegen.Title": "Health Regen",
    "UI.FTUE.RespawningLocationNoBed": "If you have claimed a bed you'll return there, otherwise you'll be taken to the temple.  ",
    "UI.FTUE.CraftingStationText": "Interact with workbenches to create new tools and weapons, as well as repairing old ones.",
    "UI.FTUE.BackpackText": "Items and resources will be stored in your backpack. Try not to overburden yourself by carrying too much",
    "UI.FTUE.BuildingMaterialsTitle": "Planks",
    "UI.FTUE.PowerLevels.Title": "Power Levels",
    "UI.FTUE.FirstArmorEquipTitle": "Power level ",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessBuildMenu": "Press {BuildMenuButton} to open the build menu.",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessInventory": "Press {InventoryButton} to interact with your inventory.",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessSpells": "Press {SpellBookButton} to open the spell book",
    "UI.FTUE.Cooking.Text": "Raw food is rarely edible, build a campfire to cook food on. A good meal will improve your health and stamina.",
    "UI.FTUE.Repair.Title": "Repairing",
    "UI.FTUE.RepairingItemsTitle": "Repairing Items",
    "UI.FTUE.RespawningTitle": "Respawning",
    "UI.FTUE.RuneCraftingTitle": "Rune Crafting",
    "UI.FTUE.RuneEssenceTitle": "Rune Essence",
    "UI.FTUE.RuneEssenceText": "Runes are crafted using rune essence, which can be mined at rune geysers all over the land.",
    "UI.FTUE.RuneCraftingText": "Runes can be crafted from rune essence at a rune altar.",
    "UI.FTUE.CastSpells": "Select a spell to cast it.",
    "UI.FTUE.Beds.Claim.Title": "Shelter from the night",
    "UI.FTUE.Beds.Shelter.Title": "Shelter from the night",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessSkills.Title": "Skills",
    "UI.FTUE.Beds.Claim.Text": "Sleeping will allow you to skip the night and alleviate fatigue.",
    "UI.FTUE.Beds.Shelter.Text": "Some structures require a roof overhead. Make sure your giving yourself sufficient shelter.",
    "UI.FTUE.SpellsAndRunesTitle": "Spells and Runes",
    "UI.FTUE.SpellsAndRunesText": "Spells require runes to cast them. They can be crafted using rune essence.",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Stability.Title": "Stability",
    "UI.FTUE.FirstNightText": "The cold will lower your stamina, and the temperature drops harshly at night. Build a campfire to keep yourself warm.",
    "UI.FTUE.UpgradingWorkstationsTitle": "Upgrading Workstations",
    "UI.FTUE.UpgradingWorkstationsText": "Upgrading a workstation increases its functionality, allowing you to craft better equipment. ",
    "UI.FTUE.RepairingItemsText": "When an item breaks you can repair it at a crafting station.",
    "UI.FTUE.HealthRegen": "When your health isn't as good as it could be, a good meal will help restore you and bolster you for the journey ahead.",
    "UI.FTUE.CraftingStationTitle": "Workbenches",
    "UI.FTUE.NeedStrongerAxeText": "Yeah, your axe isn't going to cut it – pardon the pun – against a tree like that. You'll need a stronger axe. ",
    "UI.FTUE.Encumbered": "You are carrying too much. Keep an eye on the weight of everything in your inventory.",
    "UI.FTUE.BuildingMaterialsText": "You can convert logs into wooden planks, which can be used to construct a shelter. ",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessMap": "You can open/close the map at any time by pressing {MapButton}.",
    "UI.FTUE.Repair.Text": "You can repair weapons, tools and armor at a workbench, using resources you've gathered.",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Placement.Text": "You can rotate and adjust the distance and height of a building piece before you place it.",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Stability.Text": "You can't build just anywhere. Make sure your structure is stable enough to support itself. Structures are more stable if build near the ground.",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Unlocked.2.Text": "You need a workbench to craft tools.",
    "UI.FTUE.RespawningText": "You'll be whisked to safety on death, but your items will be left behind. {DescribeRespawningLocation}",
    "UI.FTUE.AccessJournal": "You've discovered a new recipe. Press {JournalButton} to see it in the journal.",
    "UI.FTUE.FirstArmorEquipText": "Your power level can be viewed in your inventory next to your equipped armour. The higher your power level, the better your chance of survival.",
    "UI.FTUE.PowerLevels.Text": "You’re entering an area with stronger creatures and enemies. Craft better weapons and armour to improve your chances of survival.",
    "UI.FTUE.Skills.Menu.Open": "to open Skills menu",
    "UI.FTUE.Backpack.Menu.Open": "to open inventory",
    "UI.FTUE.Building.Menu.Open": "to open the Build menu"
  },
  "ST_GameplayEffects": {
    "SoulRift.FTUE.ImarusGazeStage2": "Imaru draws closer, find a Purification Pool to remove Soul Rift before its too late.",
    "SoulRift.FTUE.ImarusGazeStage1": "Imaru smells your soul, find a Purification Pool and remove Soul Rift before she finds you.",
    "SoulRift.ImarusGaze": "Imaru's Gaze",
    "SoulRift.FTUE.PreventTeleport": "Imaru's gaze prevents you from teleporting. ",
    "SoulRift.FTUE.ImarusGazeStage3": "Intertact with a Purification Pool to remove the Soul Rift state.",
    "Wither.GameplayEffect.Name": "Soul Rift",
    "SoulRift.FTUE.MissedPool": "Use your compass to find the closest Purification Pool.",
    "SoulRift.FTUE.FirstInstance": "You have become soul-rifted, and gained the attention of Imaru."
  },
  "ST_GenericDialog": {
    "CharacterNameExistsErrorBody": "A character with this name already exists. Please choose a different name or go back and delete the existing character.",
    "EOSMoreInfoHeader": "About Epic Online Services",
