  },
  "ST_GoblinDiplomacy": {
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_3": "A prophecy is like a parasite, burrowing into your soul. Twisting your choices to get its own way.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_BothAmuletsFound_3": "A prophecy is like a parasite, burrowing into your soul. Twisting your choices to get its own way.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_GivenSteak_1": "Ah, you're alright human. Not as ugly on the inside as ya is on the outside.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Bandos_5": "Armadyl slew Bandos, leaving the universe in a better state. I do not regret his passing. Gielinor is better for it.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Bandos_1": "Bandos was a war god. The Big High War God, in the parlance of my people. He delighted in conflict, battle and bloodshed.",
    "Objective4": "Bring both amulets to Zanik.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Puppet_4": "But... Bandos' mark still dug deep into my being and when he died... well, so did I.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_Default1": "Careful, this whole area is full of goblins and not the nice kind like me. What brings you all the way out here?",
    "PlayerChoice_DarkerThings": "Darker powers?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_Default2": "Do you feel it too? Prophecy. A god's backup plan, waiting for a host to sink its tendrils into.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_QuestComplete_4": "Do you think they'd object to me taking notes of their rituals? They probably would, right? Dagnammit.",
    "PlayerChoice_RefuseToHandOverSteak": "Don't hand over steak",
    "Objective6": "Find someone that can identify the Bandosian amulet.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress_NoSteak": "Go, on, do me a solid and bring me a nice steak? I'll tell ya where they hides their treasure if you do.",
    "Title": "Goblin Diplomacy",
    "PlayerChoice_HandOverSteak": "Hand over the steak",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Bandos_2": "He came to our world, Gielinor, and ignited war. Laughing all the while at the carnage.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Bandos_4": "He challenged the god of justice, Armadyl, and the two raced to build a god-killing weapon. Armadyl finished his first.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Bandos_3": "He was banished, like all the gods, with Guthix's edicts. Then returned after Guthix died to immediately pick a fight.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_5": "Here, I'll take those from you. I know how to dispose of prophecies.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_BothAmuletsFound_4": "Here, I'll take those from you. I know how to dispose of these.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_NotInvestigated_2": "How's I know? I smells it on ya mate, you stinky of theivery. Probably nicked something shiny from the other tribe.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_NoProgress_1": "How's the investigation going? Found anything yet?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundInvestigatedOther_1": "How's the investigation going? Found anything yet?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_1": "How's the investigation going? Found anything yet?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NonSwampAmuletFound_Default_1": "Hrmm, It's a prophecy alright, one of Bandos' safeguards. I've felt it before... when he made me his puppet.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundOneAmuletAndInvestigatedOther_2": "Hrmm, It's feels like a prophecy, one of Bandos' safeguards. I've felt it before... when he made me his puppet.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundSwampAmuletOnly_2": "Hrmm, It's feels like a prophecy, one of Bandos' safeguards. I've felt it before... when he made me his puppet.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Puppet_2": "I died, got resurrected and my soul was marked by his claim. I had no choice in the matter.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NonSwampAmuletFound_RuinAmuletFound_1": "I feel it down south toward the guild... and now on you? What have you found?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NonSwampAmuletFound_GuildAmuletFound_1": "I feel it up by the ruin over there, beneath this outlook,.. and now on you? What have you found?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress1": "I feel it up there by the northeast ruin, down there, you can see it from this lookout. Another presence south toward the guild, beyond a broken bridge. ",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_FoundRuinAmulet": "I felt the other presence further south around the guild.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_FoundGuildAmulet": "I felt the other presence near the ruin to the northeast.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Puppet_1": "I hate the romantic notion of destiny. Mine was to be the puppet of the goblin god of war, Bandos.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Goblins_4": "I look at goblins and see what we were and sometimes I'd like them to see who they *could* be.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Puppet_5": "I mean, I got better, but still, these things haunt you.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Puppet_3": "I nearly became something awful, but a friend helped me resist Bandos and put a stop to his scheme.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundSwampAmuletOnly_4": "I sensed something up there by the ruin over there, beneath this outlook, and south toward the guild.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress3": "I'm vulnerable to prophecy, I was Bandos' puppet for a while and I can't risk that again. Never again.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundInvestigatedOther_4": "I've been tracking a strange presence in the swamps, not far from the northeast ruins. You need to find the other piece, and quickly. There might be darker powers at work.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_GivenSteak_Ruin": "If you want to get yer hand on this lot's stuff, you'll want to look behind them barrels and crates. Not good at hiding things this lot.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_GivenSteak_Guild": "If you want to get yer hand on this lot's stuff, you'll want to look behind them vines near the old fireplace.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_NotInvestigated_3": "If you'd got here sooner, I'd help you find this lot's stuff. But that weird garou-beastmen nutjob got here first. Weird fella, lives in a cave in the swamp. ",
    "Objective2b": "Investigate the guild south of Zanik.",
    "Objective2a": "Investigate the ruin northeast of Zanik.",
    "Objective1": "Investigate the ruins to the northeast and the guild to the south of Zanik.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_3": "It's a prophecy alright, one of Bandos' safeguards. Although, since he's dead, who else might use it?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_QuestComplete_1": "It's actually quite fascinating being here, without a prophecy to worry about.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NonSwampAmuletFound_Default_2": "It's only half of the magic though. We need to find both pieces.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_4": "It's only half of the magic though. We need to find both pieces.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_DarkerPowers_2": "Let's just stop this nonsense before we meet them.",
    "Objective5": "Look for the other amulet at either the ruins northeast of Zanik, or the guild to the south.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_NoProgress_2": "No? You'll want to investigate over by the ruin over there, beneath this outlook, and south toward the guild.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundNotInvestigatedOther_2": "Oh, wait, that amulet, that's the source of the uncomfortable feeling I felt.",
    "Objective3": "Search for the other amulet piece in an area filled with mud and stagnant swampwater.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress2": "Something dangerous is hidden out here. It's sealed for now, probably in an amulet or something but we need to find it. By we, I mean you.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_6": "Take this, a little something for your trouble. A reminder that we're all masters of our own fate.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_BothAmuletsFound_5": "Take this, a little something for your trouble. A reminder that we're all masters of our own fate.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundSwampAmuletOnly_3": "That's only half of it though, you should track down the other piece. I would, but I'm vulnerable to prophecy, this is all on you.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundInvestigatedOther_2": "The amulet was missing? The reliquary filled with fetid water and mud?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_QuestComplete_2": "The goblins round here are so different from those back home, they don't even worship Bandos.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundOneAmuletAndInvestigatedOther_3": "The other's one's missing? Very disconcerting, you should track it down. I would, but I'm vulnerable to prophecy, this is all on you.",
    "Reliquery_SecondOneFound": "The reliquary has already been opened and the contents removed. There are claw marks along the outside and traces of stagnant water and mud within. Perhaps someone nearby saw something.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Goblins_2": "The war god hated anything that wasn't combat. So where the surface goblins stagnated, we cave goblins thrived.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_DarkerPowers_1": "There are always darker powers. There are things worse than gods... older than the gods.",
    "Reliquery_FirstOneFound_SecondPass": "There is nothing there but dust. ",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_QuestComplete_3": "They follow the dragons instead, which is really interesting. I wonder if it changes how their society lives?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Goblins_1": "Truth is, I'm a cave goblin -- a different tribe. We escaped Bandos' efforts in the god wars and forged a life of our own.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress_Steak": "Wait, I smell steak on ya? If you hand it over I'll tell you where they hide their secret stuff.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundOneAmuletAndInvestigatedOther_1": "Wait... I sense something on you. What's that you've got? Let me see.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_FoundSwampAmuletOnly_1": "Wait... I sense something on you. What's that you've got? Let me see.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Goblins_3": "We chose peace. Peace and understanding, and now cave goblin society is wonderfully advanced.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_4": "We should all forge our own paths, don't you think?",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress_2": "Well if you're gonna interrupt me, why not grab me some food, eh? Cos, like, I'm proper starvin right now.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_RefuseSteak": "Well, fine! No steak, no secrets! See if I care.",
    "PlayerChoice_AskAboutPuppet": "What do you mean you were a puppet?",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_NoProgress_1": "What you want? Can't you see I'm busy plotting me escape?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_2": "Whatever that druid was trying to do, I'm glad you stopped it. It would definitely not have ended well.",
    "PlayerChoice_Bandos": "Who was Bandos?",
    "PlayerChoice_OtherGoblins": "Why aren't you like the other goblins?",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_OneAmuletFoundInvestigatedOther_3": "Why would someone take it? Don't they need both pieces for the prophecy... unless...",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_BothAmuletsFound_2": "Wow, yup, definitely a prophecy. Contained in two amulet pieces, some real nasty work.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_ThisLocation": "Yeah, nick their stuff! That'll teach 'em.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_NotInvestigated_RuinGoblin": "You can take a look behind all them barrels and crates . But won't be nothing there.",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_NotInvestigated_GuildGoblin": "You can take a look behind them vines near the old fireplace . But won't be nothing there.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_BothAmuletsFound_1": "You did it! I knew you could!",
    "Reliquery_NotEnoughSpace": "You discover a strange amulet in the reliquary, but your inventory is too full to pick it up right now.",
    "Reliquery_FirstOneFound": "You find an amulet marked with the symbol of Bandos, the goblin war god. ",
    "Goblin_GoblinDiplomacy_FoundOneAmulet_NotInvestigated_1": "You lookin to steal stuff? Well's your a bit too late.",
    "Zanik_GoblinDiplomacy_Intro_BothAmuletsFound_1": "You've got the stink of divine manipulation on you, what have you discovered. May I look?",
    "Description": "Zanik needs you to stop a prophecy before it's too late."
  },
  "ST_HeartStrings": {
    "SixthMemorial5": "A shield against a shadowy emptiness. My void knight.",
    "FinalMemorial5": "As the last words leave your lips, the seed shivers and shudders to the song. It twists, stretches and transforms into a bow of glittering crystal.",
    "SixthMemorial3": "Cleddyf guthix ydym ni  \r\nNi yw'r golau treiddgar  \r\nYr ydm yma\r\nI drechu pob cysgod. I Gielinor!",
    "SixthMemorial2": "Clwych curo’r drymiau rhyfel,  A ffanffer Guthix yn canu   \r\n\r\nI imagined your war-song as you lead your Wild Knights into battle.",
    "ThirdMemorial4": "Creaduriaid. Adfeilion.   \r\n\r\nMonsters and desolation, everywhere we looked. Yet somehow we made a home, a ramshackle house of nonsense, that became my paradise.",
    "FinalMemorial4": "Dw i'n dy garu di'n fawr.",
    "FirstMemorial3": "Er mwyn tynged Gilinor. Oh Gielinor  Mae’n daith un ffordd i fewn i’r affwys, i Gilinor   \r\n\r\nThat’s why you left me. Not the ravage of time. Not the cruelty of fire-red hair turning the silver-grey of burnt-out ash. You had a mission, a journey, to take the fight into the abyss.",
    "FifthMemorial2": "Every time you stepped out the door, it was as if time took some of you from me. In barely a handful of years your limbs stiffened, you fire-red hair turned grey and you lost some of the agility you had been so proud of.",
    "QuestDescription": "Follow an elven bard's trail of memory, and discover a harmonious weapon.",
    "SecondMemorial1": "Gadael pob peth ar ôl    \r\n\r\nLeaving everything behind, I thought only I did that.",
    "QuestName": "Heartstrings",
    "FinalMemorial1": "I laid your bones to rest beneath this tree, far from our home. I felt you deserved one last adventure, stretched out across our little world.",
    "FirstMemorial1": "I never liked your story. Child of a farmer, given over to the Wild Knights, because of the fire in your eyes. It felt as if you were owed a greater story, one that could deliver even a fraction of your courage.",
    "MesaMemorial5": "I will start at our tree, in the east. Do you see it, down there, framed perfectly in this spot? A single point of brilliant blue, in an ocean of fiery red. An outsider, just like I was, until I met you.",
    "MesaMemorial4": "I wrote a song about you, about the time we spent together. It’s a technique of my people, turning music into craft. I will play the pieces of it, as I take this goodbye walk.",
    "FinalMemorial3": "I'm sorry, Meya, even now I cannot say goodbye. So let me just say the words that mean the most.",
    "MesaMemorial3": "It’s time for me to leave this place. To close this chapter on our memories and to start a life without you. I need to find myself again, without your shadow smiling out of the corner of my eye.",
    "ThirdMemorial2": "I’m still not sure why we chose this land. Brynmoor was much calmer.",
    "SecondMemorial4": "Marhog Gwagle! I Gielinor! \r\nMarchog Gwagle! Marchog! I Gielinor!   \r\n\r\nA brave warrior, defender of the world. Defeated by a tree.",
    "Memorial": "Memorial",
    "FirstMemorial5": "My journey continues eastward, following the blue in a sea made from waves of colourful dancing leaves. Saying my farewell, each footstep at a time. ",
    "SecondMemorial3": "Not you though. I remember sitting alone in the forests, wolves circling me, and then a loud crash, boisterous laughter and a mad-woman in leaf-covered armour falls out of a tree and says hello.",
    "PlayerChoice_SingSong": "Sing the bard's song of rememberance.",
    "FirstMemorial2": "So I wrote this song to conjure up the essence of you, rather than the fact. A bard’s prerogative, evoke the feelings you left in others, rather than record your daily toils.",
    "Playerchoice_Stepaway": "Step Away",
    "FourthMemorial4": "Then we were alone, just you and me. I was used to the solitude, it’s instilled into my people, but it broke my heart when I saw you were used to it too.",
    "FinalMemorial2": "This song was written for you... In memory of you. Yet the lump in my throat is so great, I cannot sound the words.",
    "MesaMemorial2": "This view feels so different without you by my side. The angle is strange, because my shoulder isn’t weighed by your head as you lean on me and sigh softly. A hundred years without you, and yet this view still feels wrong.",
    "FifthMemorial1": "To an elf time is a fickle thing, we age so much slower that time passes almost without meaning. A year to us is a heartbeat, a decade is nothing but a brief rest, a century can be as easily forgotten as any other time. But not for you.",
    "FirstMemorial4": "Trefn elitaidd rhyfelwyr affwysol   \r\n\r\nLeaving me behind, so that you could save us all.",
    "SecondMemorial2": "Wanderlust overcame reason and I journeyed across the ocean to find myself. Ashenfall is no place for an elf. There is no crystal, save what I brought with me, and the humans here distrust all outsiders. Not without reason.",
    "ThirdMemorial1": "We found a home here, together, the Wild Knight and her strange elf bard. We took the logs from the forests, and the stone from the mountain’s floor, so that we might craft a little place where we could escape together.",
    "SecondMemorial5": "We shared a meal. I told stories and you listened in a way that no one has ever listened before. All of you, every part of your being, focused on my words. I think I loved you even then, though it would be years before I realised it.",
    "FourthMemorial1": "When the war turned against your people, you took my hand and led me away. As ancient monsters left the secrecy of their shadows to inflict horror on us all.",
    "ThirdMemorial5": "Y baradwys\r\n\r\nOur world of adventure and excitement, held between four small walls.",
    "ThirdMemorial3": "Y byd dirdro. Tir llygredig   \r\n\r\nGhornfell is a harsh place, filled with dangers. The land itself is twisted, poison to the east and storms to the west. Overhead the dread Velgar circles, laughing at the destruction he’s wrought.",
    "FourthMemorial2": "Y dragonkin    \r\n\r\nI had thought them a myth, relegated to the most obscure bardic tales and songs. A shadow-on-the-wall horror story to scare small children into bed.",
    "FifthMemorial3": "Y pyrth hynaf,  \r\nar goll   \r\n\r\nThose elder gates, stealing more of you from me.",
    "FifthMemorial4": "Yet, even as time left its wounds in your skin, you were still the most beautiful creature in all of Gielinor.",
    "SixthMemorial1": "You didn’t die, you just went off to battle. That’s how I could brave the years. In the songs I wrote about you, you were off to war, fighting for Guthix against all the evils in creation.",
    "NotEnoughInventory": "You don't have enough space for the crystal seed to grow into the bow. You will need to make some room before it can do so. ",
    "MesaMemorial1": "You find a crystal in the shape of a seed. The memorial stone changes as you hold the crystal up, revealing text in elvish.",
    "SixthMemorial4": "You were Guthix’s sword, his piercing light against the darkness. That’s why you left me. Not because of time. Not because you were never coming back. But because you needed to save us all from the monsters in the night.",
    "FourthMemorial3": "“Be good little child, or the dragonkin will get you”. But, no, here they are, with their great dragon army, wiping out everyone we have ever known."
  },
  "ST_HighlightingTheProblem": {
    "WizardStatue_GotOrb5": "*THWACK*",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_WrongAnswer": "...No... nothing happens. Did you expect something to happen? Your ancestors are embarrassed by you.",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_RightAnswer1": "A panel in the statue slides aside and you retrieve a crystal orb from within. A voice from nowhere fills your head.",
    "WizardStatue_Intro1": "A statue dedicated to the wizard Ramus Lumen. A dragonkin symbol has been scratched into the plaque. A word summons itself to the tip of your tongue.",
    "WizardStatue_NoPassword": "A statue dedicated to the wizard Ramus Lumen. An unknown dragonkin symbol has been scratched into the plaque.",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_RightAnswer2": "Ah, hello, this thing on? Apprentice, well done, you've got yourself an orb. This is the first step toward creating your very own magical staff.",
    "WizardStatue_NotGotPassword_GenericAnswer": "Alas, the statue does not respond. ",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_RightAnswer3": "All you need to do is to charge the orb on the pedestals around the guild. You can find them on the towers, but you'll need to work out how to reach them yourself.",
    "WizardStatue_GotOrb1": "Alright, it's recording. Hello apprentice, well done on charging up that orb.",
    "OrbDescCharged": "An orb obtained from a statue in the Magic Institute, charged with magical energy.",
    "OrbDesc": "An orb obtained from a statue in the Magic Institute.",
    "WizardStatue_NoInventorySpace": "Don't ask me how I know this, I'm just a recording, but your bag seems a bit overburdened. Come back here once you've cleared up some space. ",
    "QuestDescription": "Explore the RuneCrafting Guild to discover the means to craft a powerful magical weapon.",
    "Objective3": "Find a way to charge the  mysterious orb.",
    "QuestTitle": "Highlighting the Problem",
    "VaultHunterJournal": "I've been searching for weeks and yet still I've found nothing. My notes have led me here, to a secret hidden within these ruins, and this statue must be the key.   \r\n\r\nThe goblins make investigation difficult and I am running out of arrows, but I know there's something here.   \r\n\r\nPrevious reports suggest there's an ancient vault nearby. A dragonkin structure full of secrets. Perhaps it might go someway to explain this symbol scratched across this statue's plaque. If I can find the entrance and make my way past its defences, perhaps I can find the answers I seek.   \r\n\r\nThere are so few of us left now, fate owes us this one.",
    "Objective1": "Investigate the area for clues about the statue.",
    "Objective_AfterDiscoveringVaultStatue": "Locate the statue near a tower and give it the password.",
    "OrbNameCharged": "Mysterious Orb [Charged]",
    "OrbName": "Mysterious Orb [Uncharged]",
    "Voice": "Mysterious Voice",
    "WizardStatue_GotOrb4": "Now Jules, turn this thing off so I can hit you with this broom without it being preserved for future generations.",
    "WizardStatue_GotOrb3": "Now we just attach the orb to the shaft and voila, one staff of light. Great job, apprentice!",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_RightAnswer4": "Once you've charged the orb at all three, bring it back here to create your staff.",
    "PlayerChoice_Incorrect_NotFoundPassword1": "Open Sesame",
    "PlayerChoice_Incorrect_NotFoundPassword2": "Password",
    "Pedestal": "Pedestal",
    "PlayerChoice_Incorrect1": "Pigeontoothpick",
    "PlayerChoice_Correct": "Pthentorok",
    "PlayerChoice_Incorrect2": "Pythontworocks",
    "Objective4": "Return to the wizard statue.",
    "PlayerChoice_Incorrect_NotFoundPassword3": "Saradomin Smells",
    "Objective2": "Search the Runecrafting Guild for a statue.",
    "Statue": "Statue",
    "WizardStatue_GotPassword_RightAnswer5": "That's done, right, how do I turn this thing off? Is it this button he--",
    "Pedestal_Orb_FullyCharged": "The orb hums with power. Time to return to the statue.",
    "Pedestal_HasOrb_AlreadyUsed": "The pedestal has no charge left.",
    "VaultStatue_Used": "The statue is dormant. ",
    "WizardStatie_PostQuest": "The statue remains silent. ",
    "Pedestal_DoesNotHaveOrb": "There seems to be space for a sphere of some kind.",
    "WizardStatue_GotOrb2": "This orb is the heart of a very special staff known as the Staff of Light. Popular with blue robed wizards throughout Saradomin's domain.",
    "VaultHunterJournal_Title": "Vault Hunter's Journal",
    "Pedestal_HasOrb_NotUsedYet": "You place the orb on the pedestal. Ambient energy is absorbed by the orb, causing it to glow faintly. The pedestal loses its charge.",
    "VaultStatue_Intro1": "Your thoughts swirl with images of a statue by the Runecrafting Guild. A word leaps to the front of your mind -- Pthentorok"
  },
