  "ST_LoadingScreen": {
    "ui.loading.body3": "During the Third Age, Gielinor became the battleground for a conflict between the gods. Mighty armies battled one another for control over powerful artefacts, such as the Stone of Jas and the God Sword – a weapon rumoured to be powerful enough to kill a god. \r\n\r\nThe God Wars ended when the God of Chaos, Zamorak, used the Stone to set off a destructive blast that wiped the region of Forinthry from the map – creating what is now referred to as The Wilderness. ",
    "ui.loading.body4": "It is unknown why the people of Gielinor crave these paper hats, yet people have been murdered over them. There are no smiths, nor artisans of the modern age that seem to be able to recreate these designs, deceptively simple as they are. \r\n\r\nTo this day, Santa regrets simply giving them away. If he'd just kept a handful, he might not be struggling to deal with his elves demand for a payrise. ",
    "ui.loading.loading": "LOADING",
    "ui.loading.header4": "Party Hats",
    "ui.loading.header3": "The God Wars",
    "ui.loading.header1": "The Sixth Age",
    "ui.loading.header2": "The Wise Old Man",
    "ui.loading.body1": "The history of Gielinor is split into different ages, each representing a major event. Such as the  Third Age, the age of the God Wars. \r\n\r\nThe Sixth Age was created with the death of Guthix, the god of balance and harmony. This age has seen a new conflict between the gods that led to them being banished from Gielinor by the World Guardian. ",
    "ui.loading.body2": "The legendary hero Dioynsius is a tale whispered to dwarven children about overcoming great evil. Wall carvings by a forgotten mountain tribe show him battling monsters and returning triumphant. \r\n\r\nYet bank tellers talk of him in hushed, frightened, whispers ever since he went on a little killing spree. Never underestimate the lure of a Party Hat."
  },
